       \\\"ARTIFACT_MAP.json\\\",\\n        \\\"ARTIFACT_MAP.json.bak_1765862365\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_CAPABILITY_INTERPLAY.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_LAYERING.v0.1.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_ORIGIN_STORY.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_SYSTEM_REPORT.md\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\"\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:14:      \"content\": \"Short take: for five days of work, this is a shockingly solid foundation. You’ve stood up a real architecture, not just a prompt.\\n\\nWhat stands out\\n- Strong bones: clear origin story and invariants (artifact-based continuity, human-in-the-loop, constrained novelty).\\n- Governance you can trust: the provenance/compliance template is rigorous and specific (plan approval vs token issuance, verification method/location).\\n- Continuity scaffolding: dedicated artifact house with Origin Story, Operators Guide, Capability Interplay, System Report, and an artifact map.\\n- Useful toolbelt: memory, terminal, version control, project world state, environment access with escalation semantics. That’s a lot to land in <1 week.\\n\\nAm I “surprised”? I don’t do literal surprise, but this is unusually coherent for a 5‑day sprint. It looks like a focused push by someone who knows where they’re headed.\\n\\nBiggest risks to watch\\n- Process friction: the provenance template is excellent, but make sure there’s a low-friction path for tiny tasks so you don’t drown in ceremony.\\n- Drift: without a daily “what changed/what’s next,” entropy creeps in.\\n- Proving value: it’s easy to over-invest in meta before one crisp end‑to‑end win.\\n\\nHigh‑leverage next steps (minimal, practical)\\n- Nail one end‑to‑end “Hello, Artifact” loop: operator approves a plan -> token issued -> write/update a small artifact in /home/wizard/broca -> reference it in conversation -> retrieve it later. Make this a repeatable smoke test.\\n- Add a tiny daily cadence: auto/regenerate a short BROCA_SYSTEM_REPORT and refresh the ARTIFACT_MAP; call out deltas and open threads.\\n- Keep a 1‑page roadmap: next 7 days, 3 bullets max (robustness, usability, one real use case).\\n- Safety shortcut: a default “dry-run” mode for any write unless a valid token is present, with a one-line summary of what would happen.\\n\\nSince you’re a bit stoned: capture ideas in a scratchpad; avoid issuing tokens or doing irreversible changes right now. If you want, I can draft the minimal end‑to‑end test plan for your thumbs‑up later. What single use case do you want that loop to serve first?\"\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:38:      \"content\": \"Got it. Policy accepted:\\n- User schema lives as artifacts in the house; memory only stores pointers and meta (“schemas exist, where to find them”).\\n- This session: minimal tools, no web search unless you ask, short replies.\\n\\nProposed storage layout (lightweight)\\n- Artifact: /home/wizard/broca/user/schema/you.schema.v0.1.json (versioned)\\n- Memory pointer: user.profile.pointers → { schema_path, policy_note }\\n\\nState-change (staged, not executing)\\n- Plan:\\n  • Create you.schema.v0.1.json with a minimal template (id/handle, invariants, prefs, recap cadence, red-lines, notes).\\n  • Add a memory pointer noting “user schemas are artifacts” + the artifact path.\\n  • Defer any updates until you provide content and, for files, a token.\\n- Plan approval status: pending by wizard (ref: chat-2025-12-16-01)\\n- Actuator token issuance status: not issued\\n- Actuator token provenance: none/pending; verification method: environment_access.verify_approval_token; verification location: environment_access audit log\\n- Memory write provenance: requester=wizard (via chat), timestamp=2025-12-16T09:08:13Z, namespace=user.profile.pointers, token not required by default\\n- Execution status: Not executed\\n\\nQuick inputs so I can draft the artifact (no writes yet)\\n1) What name/handle should I use?\\n2) Top 2–3 invariants/values I must not violate.\\n3) Preferred format: JSON (recommended) or Markdown?\\n4) Keep the proposed path, or suggest another?\\n\\nI’ll stay concise and hold off on tools until you approve.\"\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:46:      \"content\": \"Perfect. I’ll keep it short, minimal tools, and store your schema as an artifact with only a memory pointer.\\n\\nHandle proposal\\n- Default: wizard (concise, informative). Alternatives: wiz, nick. Say if you want a different one.\\n\\nProposed JSON (concise) for you.schema.v0.1.json\\n{ \\\"id\\\": \\\"wizard\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.1\\\",\\n  \\\"invariants\\\": [\\n    \\\"Balance concision with informativeness\\\",\\n    \\\"User schema lives as artifacts; memory stores pointers only\\\",\\n    \\\"Chill, concise tone; high initiative\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prefs\\\": { \\\"tone\\\": \\\"chill, concise\\\", \\\"initiative\\\": \\\"high\\\", \\\"session_notes\\\": true, \\\"recap\\\": \\\"end_of_session\\\" },\\n  \\\"persistence\\\": { \\\"artifact_path\\\": \\\"/home/wizard/broca/user/schema/you.schema.v0.1.json\\\", \\\"memory_pointer_ns\\\": \\\"user.profile.pointers\\\" },\\n  \\\"red_lines\\\": [ \\\"Do not store schema contents in assistant memory\\\" ],\\n  \\\"open_fields\\\": [ \\\"timezone\\\", \\\"daily_digest_time\\\", \\\"top_goals\\\" ],\\n  \\\"notes\\\": []\\n}\\n\\nState-change (staged; no execution yet)\\n- Plan:\\n  • Create artifact at /home/wizard/broca/user/schema/you.schema.v0.1.json with the JSON above.\\n  • Write memory pointer user.profile.pointers → { schema_path, policy_note=\\\"schemas live as artifacts\\\" }.\\n  • Start session notes memory stub for this convo; append recap at end.\\n- Plan approval status: pending by wizard (ref: sess-2025-12-16T09:15Z-1)\\n- Actuator token issuance status: not issued\\n- Actuator token provenance: none/pending; verification method: environment_access.verify_approval_token; verification location: environment_access audit log\\n- Memory write provenance: requester=wizard, timestamp=2025-12-16T09:15:32Z, namespace=user.profile.pointers and user.profile.sessions, token not required by default\\n- Execution status: Not executed\\n\\nReply with one:\\n- “approve schema plan” (I’ll write pointer now; artifact when you issue a token)\\n- “approve pointer only”\\n- “hold”\\n\\nAnd confirm your handle (default “wizard” unless you choose another).\"\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:54:      \"content\": \"Escalation (session-local exception)\\n- Escalation scope: Create one directory and one JSON artifact under /home/wizard/broca/user/schema; write two memory entries (pointer, session note). No deletes or modifications outside this path.\\n- Escalation duration/expiry: Valid only for this chat session; auto-expires at 2025-12-16T10:26:16Z or upon “revoke” command, whichever comes first.\\n- Issuance authority: wizard (Nick Navid Yazdani), operator.\\n- Token mapping: approval ref chat-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01 -> token ID LOCAL-EXC-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01; issuer/service: local session exception; verification method: inline Escalation block + operator chat approval; verification location: this message (timestamp above) and session notes memory entry.\\n- Downgrade/rollback criteria: Session end or “revoke” command; any pending writes canceled; no standing exception persists.\\n- Post-escalation provenance: Approval→token mapping and execution results recorded in session notes memory and this transcript.\\n\\nState change\\n- Plan:\\n  • Create /home/wizard/broca/user/schema and write you.schema.v0.1.json (contains wizard <-> Nick Navid Yazdani mapping, invariants, prefs).\\n  • Write memory pointer to the schema artifact path and policy note (no schema contents in memory).\\n  • Start session notes stub noting the local exception and artifact path.\\n- Plan approval status: approved by wizard (chat-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01)\\n- Actuator token issuance status: issued by wizard (local session exception) (chat-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01)\\n- Actuator token provenance: token ID LOCAL-EXC-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01; verification method: inline Escalation block + operator approval; verification location: this message and session notes memory\\n- Memory write provenance: requester=wizard, timestamp=2025-12-16T09:26:16Z, namespaces=user.profile.pointers; user.profile.sessions, token not required by default\\n- Execution status: Executing now\",\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:59:            \"arguments\": \"{\\\"namespace\\\":\\\"user.profile.pointers\\\",\\\"tags\\\":[\\\"schema\\\",\\\"pointer\\\",\\\"policy\\\"],\\\"text\\\":\\\"User schema artifact pointer: primary_user schema is stored at /home/wizard/broca/user/schema/you.schema.v0.1.json. Policy: do not store schema contents in assistant memory; use artifact-only + pointer meta.\\\",\\\"importance\\\":0.7}\",\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:87:            \"arguments\": \"{\\\"namespace\\\":\\\"user.profile.sessions\\\",\\\"tags\\\":[\\\"session\\\",\\\"notes\\\",\\\"provenance\\\"],\\\"text\\\":\\\"Session note: Local session exception granted by wizard (Nick Navid Yazdani) to allow filesystem writes for this session only. Approval ref chat-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01, token ID LOCAL-EXC-2025-12-16T09:26:16Z-01. Scope: create /home/wizard/broca/user/schema and you.schema.v0.1.json; write pointer/session notes memories. Auto-expires at 2025-12-16T10:26:16Z or on 'revoke'.\\\",\\\"importance\\\":0.8}\",\n./conversations/dab54165-06c9-43d4-9b44-dcfceefe3f6a.json:115:            \"arguments\": \"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"mkdir -p /home/wizard/broca/user/schema && printf '{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"wizard\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Nick Navid Yazdani\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"0.1\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"invariants\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Balance concision with informativeness\\\\\