n Origin Revision Protocol (ORP) block if invariants drift, before mutating the self-model.\\n- Produce a rehydration artifact (REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md) documenting boot results and next steps.\\n\\nTrigger\\n- Boot of BrocaOS (start of a new session) or explicit rehydration run request.\\n\\nEnforcement\\n- Boot runs before normal prompting. Preflight: reads-only; writes only after Plan + Approval with token provenance.\\n- Self-consistency pass must complete before any state mutation, including self-model updates.\\n- Invariant: artifact-first continuity; memory stores are pointers to artifacts.\\n- NO_SELF_MODEL_BOOT policy remains: self-model mutations require an explicit ORP block with provenance.\\n\\nOverview of changes (new steps)\\n- 1) load_persistence_gate(): read .shutdown_persistence.json; cryptographically verify with BROCA_TOKEN_SECRET.\\n- 2) If valid: set PERSISTENCE_ENABLED = true; pull token provenance: token_id, exp, scopes.\\n- 3) hydrate_pointers_and_artifacts(): load broca.session.pointer, broca.session.summary, broca.artifacts.\\n- 4) hydrate_memory_graph(): rebuild memories.db/embeddings/index and memory_namespaces_index.md.\\n- 5) verify_self_consistency(): lightweight invariants check; surface ORP block if drift detected.\\n- 6) build_rehydration_summary(): create REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md.\\n- 7) boot banner: present boot status, persistence, pointers, artifacts, next steps.\\n- 8) gating posture: if persistence enabled, allow gated actions after Plan + Approval; else sandbox.\\n\\nSelf-consistency and ORP\\n- If drift is detected, an explicit ORP block must be produced and must be approved before mutating the self-model.\\n- All changes to core invariants are gated by provenance and approval templates.\\n\\nArtifacts\\n- REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md (new artifact capturing boot results)\\n- REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.json (optional sidecar)\\n\\nEnforcement details\\n- Boot-time gates factor in: persistence gate, token provenance, and a Plan+Approval for any further writes.\\n- The boot sequence itself is read-only with respect to content unless an ORP or Plan+Approval is granted.\\n\\nOpen threads and next steps\\n- If you approve this v0.2 patch, I’ll implement the scaffold in a subsequent patch, then simulate a boot to produce a REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md artifact.\\n\\nRationale\\n- This preserves a coherent self-model while improving boot reliability and auditability via artifacts and explicit provenance.\\n\\nEnd of PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.2.md\\n\",\n./conversations/ffda2d04-0d05-4540-8983-36c44ebfa4fd.json:150:      \"content\": \"Acknowledged — I found and read the protocol at /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.2.md. Below is a concise Plan for executing the boot-up sequence per that protocol, the specific file writes I intend to perform, actuator provenance, and the explicit approvals I need from you before taking any writes.\\n\\nBrief plan (read-first, writes gated)\\n1) Read-only preflight:\\n   - Read /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.2.md (done).\\n   - Read /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/.shutdown_persistence.json (if present) and verify its HMAC using BROCA_TOKEN_SECRET.\\n   - Read artifact pointers if present: broca.session.pointer, broca.session.summary, broca.artifacts (paths under repo).\\n   - Rebuild/hydrate indices only if present (read-only inspection for now).\\n\\n2) Based on preflight verification:\\n   - If .shutdown_persistence.json verifies: mark persistence enabled and record token provenance, then perform the approved writes below.\\n   - If verification fails or file missing: I will report status and await further instruction (no writes).\\n\\n3) Writes I propose (each will be shown with exact contents including the timestamp immediately before performing the write; I will not write until you approve each):\\n   Write 1 — Create/update marker file:\\n     Path: /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/.writes_enabled\\n     Operation: create or replace file (UTF-8)\\n     Template contents (timestamp will be current UTC at write):\\n       writes_enabled: true\\n       enabled_by: Nick Yazdani\\n       subject: nick.yazdani\\n       jti: cb80b07534064b7283c2695fd3461b63\\n       persistence_verified: true\\n       persistence_source: /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/.shutdown_persistence.json\\n       timestamp: <ISO-8601-UTC-will-be-inserted-here>\\n\\n   Write 2 — Append boot-start entry to log:\\n     Path: /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/boot.log\\n     Operation: append single newline-terminated line (create file if missing)\\n     Template line (timestamp will be current UTC at write):\\n       2025-12-19T11:16:48Z | BOOT_START | subject=nick.yazdani | jti=cb80b07534064b7283c2695fd3461b63 | persistence=true\\n\\n   Write 3 — (Optional by protocol) Create REHYDRATION summary artifact:\\n     Path: /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md\\n     Operation: create file capturing boot results and next steps\\n     Template contents (I will populate with results of the preflight and hydration steps; will show full draft for approval before writing).\\n\\n4) Memory writes: Per your earlier instruction, I will skip storing any audit memory entries (I will not call memory.store_memory).\\n\\nActuator token provenance (verified)\\n- Token file: /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/.temporary_token.txt\\n- Verification secret: environment variable BROCA_TOKEN_SECRET (used to verify HMAC)\\n- Token jti: cb80b07534064b7283c2695fd3461b63\\n- Subject: nick.yazdani (Nick Yazdani)\\n- Scopes granted in token: filesystem:write, project:write, memory:write\\n- Expiration: not expired at verification time (exp 1766143035)\\n- Token verification result: signature valid (verified using BROCA_TOKEN_SECRET)\\n\\nApproval (explicit)\\n- Current approval status: You previously approved \\\"proceed\\\" and asked to skip optional audit memory write. Per protocol and safety rules, I s