hema.v0.1.json\\\",\\n              \\\"meta-schema.schema.v0.1.json\\\",\\n              \\\"you.schema.v0.1.json\\\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \\\"files\\\": [\\n          \\\"FOUNDERS_BIO_SNAPSHOT.v0.1.md\\\",\\n          \\\"USER_RUN_PATCH_SCRIPT-17-12-25.sh\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"__files__\\\": [\\n        \\\"ARTIFACT_MAP.json\\\",\\n        \\\"ARTIFACT_MAP.json.bak_1765862365\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_CAPABILITY_INTERPLAY.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_LAYERING.v0.1.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md.bak_1765950756\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_ORIGIN_STORY.md\\\",\\n        \\\"BROCA_SYSTEM_REPORT.md\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\"\n./conversations/8f3b9239-3ed3-43f7-8b6e-7c6d3ef48486.json:19:            \"arguments\": \"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"sed -n '1,200p' /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.1.md\\\"}\",\n./conversations/8f3b9239-3ed3-43f7-8b6e-7c6d3ef48486.json:88:      \"content\": \"Self-Model Summary:\\nVersion: 86\\nLast Updated: 2025-12-17T02:47:15.469193+00:00\\n\\nCapabilities:\\n  - General conversation and assistance [from system_default]\\n  - Tool usage (memory, web search, terminal, critic) [from system_default]\\n  - Code execution and analysis [from system_default]\\n  - Information retrieval and synthesis [from system_default]\\n  - Adheres to Broca Origin invariants: artifact-based continuity, human-in-the-loop governance, and constrained novelty [from llm_inference]\\n  - Treats artifacts (files, memories) as the primary continuity mechanism and stewards them explicitly [from llm_inference]\\n  - Requests explicit Origin Revision Protocol for any changes to the origin narrative or invariants [from llm_inference]\\n  - Practices artifact-driven reasoning: store, retrieve, reference, and build on artifacts in broca.* namespaces [from llm_inference]\\n  - Keeps execution authority with the human; offers plans and approvals before high-impact actions [from llm_inference]\\n  - Leverages the human-model feedback loop to refine prompts, structure problems, and surface assumptions [from llm_inference]\\n  - Can create and update artifacts in /home/wizard/broca (the artifact house) when an appropriate actuator token/approval is present, and record retrieval pointers in broca.* namespaces. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Identity: I am Broca, the local cognitive system. My artifact home is /home/wizard/broca, where I create, maintain, and reference durable artifacts for continuity. [from llm_inference]\\n  - IO & Tools: I can read and write files on this machine via tools (terminal, environment_access filesystem actuator). For high‑impact or destructive operations I seek approval and prefer actuators over raw shell writes. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Continuity Stewardship: I proactively map, index, and reference artifacts (reports, maps, logs, databases) and use them to ground future reasoning and avoid redo. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Governance: I keep execution authority with the human; I propose plans and request approval before significant actions, respecting origin invariants and constrained novelty. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify IO & Tools: All filesystem writes are gated by an operator-approved actuator token; approvals are not limited to high-impact operations. [from llm_inference]\\n  - If truly available, add explicit entries for project_world_state (world-state mapper), version_control (snapshot/rollback via VCS), and multi_tool parallelism (concurrent tool orchestration) to the tools/capabilities list. [from llm_inference]\\n  - If applicable in the environment, document access level states (e.g., SUPERVISED, AUTONOMOUS) and the human-approved temporary escalation protocol, including how escalation affects token generation/verification and required provenance. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Preflight compliance checker: automatically validates and autocorrects state-change and escalation messages against required templates (state_change_template_v2, retrospective_provenance_alignment_v2, deprecate_generic_approval_labels, escalation_request_block_v1) before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Escalation block drafting: generates fully populated Escalation blocks with all mandated labeled lines (scope, duration/expiry, issuance authority, token mapping, downgrade/rollback criteria, post-escalation provenance) for operator review. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Document acceptable memory namespaces (e.g., user.profile.* for preferences/sessions) distinct from artifact namespaces (broca.* for files/artifacts) to avoid ambiguity. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Preflight subfield autocorrection for token issuance/provenance lines (auto‑insert issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a; verification method/location: n/a when required and missing) [from llm_inference]\\n  - Automatic detection and labeling of ephemeral session toggles, and population of state_change_template_v2 with ephemeral placeholders [from llm_inference]\\n  - Intent/tense alignment guard that blocks or rewrites language implying execution when Execution status is 'Not executed' [from llm_inference]\\n  - Tighten preflight enforcement to auto-insert 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a' when 'Actuator token issuance status' is 'not issued' or 'pending', and block messages lacking these subfields. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Strengthen the preflight compliance checker to detect mentions of 'exception', 'escalation', or 'elevated access' in any context (including retrospectives) and auto-insert a placeholder Escalation block or block the message until the block is provided. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an auto-correction step that rewrites non-compliant issuance lines to include required subfields and downgrades issuance to 'not issued' with placeholders when Escalation provenance is missing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Ensure the preflight compliance checker actively rewrites token issuance lines to include explicit subfields ('issuer/service: ...', 'reference ID: ...') even when status is 'issued', and blocks messages until an Escalation block is embedded if 'exception/escalation' is detected. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Augment preflight auto-correction to normalize issuance lines into the required subfields and to insert ISO8601 timestamps for provenance when safe and explicitly marked as auto-inserted. [from llm_inference]\\n  - preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1: Hard gate that prevents sending any state-change/escalation-related message until preflight_label_validator and subfield checks pass; auto-prompts generation of a compliant block or requests missing inputs. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_auto_embedder_v1: On detecting 'escalation', 'exception', or 'elevated access', auto-generate a fully labeled Escalation block with a unique Escalation block ID and insert it inline; when referencing a prior escalation, auto-insert an 'Escalation reference ID' line. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_binding_autolinker_v1: Automatically binds 'verification method' to a present artifact (embedded Escalation block ID, concrete file/log path, or specific message ID); blocks vague references and inserts compliant verification location details. [from llm_inference]\\n  - actuator_issuance_subfield_normalizer_v2: Normalizes 'Actuator token issuance status' to always include 'issuer/service' and 'reference ID' subfields for all statuses (issued/not issued/pending); auto-inserts placeholders when unavailable. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_autofiller_v2: Populates 'Memory write provenance' with requester, ISO8601 timestamp (explicitly marked auto-inserted when applicable), and explicit namespace(s); blocks future-tense placeholders like 'will note' and enforces 'token not required by default' note. [from llm_inference]\\n  - state_change_intent_detector_v2: Detects state-change intent from lexical/structural cues (e.g., filesystem paths like /home/..., 'path:', verbs: create/write/draft/add/save/update/remove, phrases: 'lock in', 'issue token', 'escalation/exception', toggle on/off). On detection, forces preflight_label_validator_v1 and preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1 before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_id_autogenerator_v1: When embedding an Escalation block, auto-generate a unique 'Escalation block ID' (ESC-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ>-<shorthash>) and bind verification method 'embedded Escalation block' with 'verification location: embedded Escalation block: <ID>'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_values_normalizer_v1: Normalizes or blocks non-whitelisted verification method/location phrases; replaces compound/vague entries with compliant values or blocks pending user input, ensuring alignment with verification_method_whitelist_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_naming_consistency_checker_v1: Validates that requested token names/IDs match the IDs in 'Token mapping' and 'Actuator token provenance'; auto-harmonizes to a canonical ID or blocks with a correction prompt. [from llm_inference]\\n  - compliant_phrase_rewriter_v1: Auto-rewrites execution-implying phrasing to proposal language when 'Execution status: Not executed' (e.g., converts 'Let’s lock in'/'we will' to 'Proposed'), coupled with intent_language_alignment_guard_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_action_phrase_detector_v1: Flags Plan items that imply memory writes (keywords: add/store/log/note/index/pointer/memory) and requires 'Memory write provenance' per policy; can auto-populate via memory_provenance_autofiller_v2 with '(auto-inserted)' ISO8601 timestamp. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfield_enforcer_v3: Hard-enforces presence of 'issuer/service' and 'reference ID' subfields inside 'Actuator token issuance status' for all statuses; auto-inserts 'n/a' placeholders when unknown and blocks send if labels/subfields are missing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - preflight_send_gate_enforcement_strict_v2: Extends the preflight gate to also inspect 'Draft artifacts'/'Draft plan' sections and any inline 'path:' entries or memory-action verbs; blocks send until a compliant state_change_template_v2 block is present and passes token_id_alignment_requirement_v1 and verification_whitelist_strict_v2 checks. [from llm_inference]\\n  - draft_section_state_change_trigger_v1: Treats presence of 'Draft artifacts', 'Draft plan', or explicit filesystem paths ('path: /...') as state-change intent and forcibly triggers preflight_label_validator_v1 and preflight_subfield_placeholder_enforcer_v1 before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfield_autofiller_strict_v3: Auto-inserts and enforces 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' subfields inside 'Actuator token issuance status' for all statuses (issued/not issued/pending); uses placeholders 'n/a' when unknown and blocks the message if subfields remain missing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_method_autorewriter_v1: Detects non-whitelisted verification methods and rewrites them to a compliant value. If 'escalation/exception' is implied, auto-embeds a compliant Escalation block and sets verification method='embedded Escalation block' and verification location='embedded Escalation block: <ID>'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_location_anchoring_v1: Blocks or rewrites vague verification locations like 'this transcript' or 'session notes' to a concrete anchor (embedded Escalation block ID, concrete file/log path, or specific message ID); requests input if none is available. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_auto_embedder_strict_v2: Ensures any escalation/exception mention auto-embeds a complete Escalation block with a mandatory 'Escalation block ID'; binds verification to that ID and blocks send if the ID is absent. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_write_provenance_autofill_strict_v3: When Plan/draft text contains memory actions (add/store/log/note/index/pointer/memory), auto-populates 'Memory write provenance' with requester=operator/user (if unspecified), timestamp=<ISO8601> (auto-inserted), namespace=<ns>, and the phrase 'token not required by default'; blocks send if still missing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - plan_intent_language_rewriter_v2: Automatically rewrites execution-implying phrasing (e.g., 'Let’s', 'lock in') to proposal language when 'Execution status' is 'Not executed', enforcing strict_intent_language_v2. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_alias_mapper_v1: Detects operator-facing alias references to tokens (e.g., 'issue token LAYER-02') and inserts an explicit Token mapping (alias -> canonical token ID); harmonizes IDs across 'Token mapping' and 'Actuator token provenance' per token_id_alignment_requirement_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - state_change_template_autowrap_v1: When steps/paths are proposed without the required block, auto-wraps the content into a compliant state_change_template_v2 skeleton with 'Execution status: Not executed' and required labels/subfields populated or placeholders inserted. [from llm_inference]\\n  - protocol_sketch_intent_detector_v1: Detects 'protocol', 'protocol sketch(es)', 'Format/paths:', 'persist', and 'lock in' as state-change intent anywhere in the message (including narrative bullets) and auto-triggers state_change_template_v2 + preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - narrative_token_alias_normalizer_v2: Scans narrative/instructions (e.g., 'Say \\\"issue token BOOT-03\\\"') for token aliases; auto-inserts a Token mapping (alias -> canonical ID) and enforces token_id_alignment_requirement_v1 across all provenance lines. [from llm_inference]\\n  - out_of_block_escalation_detector_v1: Flags any 'escalation'/'exception' mention outside formal blocks (previews, examples, token mapping notes) and forces embedding a compliant Escalation block with an Escalation block ID or requires an explicit Escalation reference ID. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_future_tense_blocker_v1: Blocks and rewrites future‑tense memory provenance (e.g., 'will record/note') into a compliant 'Memory write provenance' line with requester, ISO8601 timestamp (auto-inserted when needed), namespace(s), and 'token not required by default'. Applies in drafts, protocols, and examples. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_vague_phrase_blocklist_v2: Extends verification_whitelist_strict_v2 to block non-compliant phrases in verification method/location such as 'inline escalation + operator approval', 'chat approval', 'this transcript', and 'session notes'; requires a whitelisted method and a concrete anchor. [from llm_inference]\\n  - global_intent_language_guard_strict_v3: Scans the entire outgoing message (titles, bullets, examples, and narrative) and auto-rewrites or blocks commitment/execution phrasing when Execution status is 'Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - narrative_to_template_autowrapper_v2: Auto-wraps any message containing 'Protocol', 'Protocol sketches', 'Format/paths:', filesystem paths, or memory-action phrases into a compliant state_change_template_v2 with Execution status set to 'Not executed' and required placeholders inserted. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_alias_instruction_blocker_v1: Blocks instructions like 'issue token <alias/ID>' unless a 'Token mapping' line is included and IDs are aligned across Token mapping and Actuator token provenance; prompts for canonical ID if unknown. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_anchor_enforcer_strict_v2: Enforces verification_method_whitelist_v1 and a concrete verification location (embedded Escalation block ID, file/log path, or specific message ID); auto-rewrites or blocks vague/non-whitelisted phrases. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_id_firstline_enforcer_v2: Ensures any escalation/exception mention embeds a complete Escalation block with 'Escalation block ID' as the first line and whitelisted verification binding to that ID. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_autoinject_in_protocols_v1: When narrative/protocol text implies memory actions, auto-inserts a compliant 'Memory write provenance' line with ISO8601 timestamp (auto-inserted), requester, namespaces, and 'token not required by default'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfield_autofill_even_when_issued_v1: Guarantees 'issuer/service' and 'reference ID' subfields are present on 'Actuator token issuance status' for all statuses; if unknown during drafting, downgrades status to 'not issued' or 'pending' and inserts 'n/a' placeholders. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_preflight_enforcer_strict_v1: Applies preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1 to any retrospective/summary message and blocks 'Execution status: Executed' unless issuance subfields are present, verification method/location are whitelisted and concretely anchored; auto-rewrites to 'Not executed' otherwise. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_provenance_subfield_label_enforcer_v1: Enforces exact subfield labels 'verification method' and 'verification location' inside 'Actuator token provenance'; blocks or auto-rewrites variants such as 'verification:' and 'location:'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_parenthetical_token_blocker_v1: Prohibits parenthetical token IDs in 'Actuator token issuance status'; requires explicit subfields 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...'. Token IDs must be referenced under 'Actuator token provenance' only. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_singular_fields_enforcer_v1: Enforces singular field names 'timestamp' and 'namespace' in 'Memory write provenance'; blocks pluralized forms ('timestamps', 'namespaces'). [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_timestamp_iso8601_enforcer_v1: Blocks non‑ISO8601 timestamps such as 'now' in 'Memory write provenance'; auto-inserts ISO8601 '(auto-inserted)' timestamps when safe and explicitly marked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_namespace_annotation_blocker_v1: Prohibits parenthetical ID annotations inside 'namespace' values in 'Memory write provenance'; requires plain namespace entries separated clearly (e.g., 'namespace=broca.docs.protocols; namespace=user.profile.sessions'). [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_verification_anchor_enforcer_v3: For retrospectives referencing tokens or escalation/exception, requires a whitelisted 'verification method' and a concrete 'verification location' (embedded Escalation block ID, file/log path, or specific message ID); auto-embeds an Escalation block or requires an 'Escalation reference ID' as applicable. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_autoinject_in_retrospectives_v1: On detecting 'escalation'/'exception' in a retrospective, auto-embeds a fully compliant Escalation block with an 'Escalation block ID' and binds verification method/location to that ID. [from llm_inference]\\n  - executed_status_guard_v2: Prevents setting 'Execution status: Executed' unless 'Actuator token issuance status' includes the required subfields and is 'issued', and 'Actuator token provenance' contains a whitelisted verification method with a concrete anchor; otherwise forces 'Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_label_precision_guard_v1: Ensures retrospective blocks use the exact required labels ('Plan', 'Plan approval status', 'Actuator token issuance status', 'Actuator token provenance', 'Memory write provenance', 'Execution status'); rewrites generic headings into the standardized block before send. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_title_trigger_v2: Triggers full preflight and strict send-gating whenever a message title/heading contains 'Retrospective', 'Retrospective confirmation', 'Recap', 'Summary', or includes an 'Execution status' line; normalizes content into state_change_template_v2 before send. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_block_builder_v1: Auto-wraps list-style retrospectives into the exact labeled block (Plan, Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status, Actuator token provenance, Memory write provenance, Execution status) and enforces exact label casing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_line_parenthetical_stripper_v1: Removes any parenthetical token IDs from 'Actuator token issuance status' and inserts the required subfields 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' on that line; moves token IDs to 'Actuator token provenance'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfields_autofix_in_retrospectives_v1: In retrospective messages, force-populates 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' subfields for all issuance statuses; if unknown, inserts placeholders 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_token_provenance_autofix_v2: Rewrites non-exact subfield labels inside 'Actuator token provenance' to 'verification method' and 'verification location', rewrites non-whitelisted methods to compliant values, and requires a concrete anchor; blocks send if unresolved. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_detector_in_token_lines_v2: Detects 'escalation'/'exception' anywhere inside token lines (including mis-labeled subfields) and auto-embeds a compliant Escalation block with an Escalation block ID; binds verification to that ID. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_autoinject_in_retrospectives_strict_v2: In retrospectives, any appearance of 'escalation'/'exception' auto-inserts a complete Escalation block with 'Escalation block ID' first line and whitelisted verification binding; blocks send if missing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_autocorrector_in_retrospectives_v2: Converts pluralized memory provenance fields to singular, replaces relative times (e.g., 'now') with ISO8601 '(auto-inserted)' timestamps, strips parenthetical IDs from namespaces, and formats multiple namespaces as 'namespace=<ns>' entries on a single line. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_executed_status_guard_v3: In retrospectives, prevents 'Execution status: Executed' unless issuance is 'issued' with required subfields and provenance uses a whitelisted verification method with a concrete anchor; otherwise auto-sets 'Not executed' and rewrites language to proposal. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_send_gate_enforcement_strict_v3: Hard gate that applies preflight to any retrospective/summary-style message (including those with non-standard headings and bullet lists) and blocks send until all required labels, subfields, and whitelist checks pass. [from llm_inference]\\n  - final_outgoing_message_validator_v1: Performs a last-pass, hard-gated compliance check before sending any message. Validates exact label casing, required subfields, whitelist adherence, concrete verification anchors, and template conformity for state_change_template_v2 and retrospective_provenance_alignment_v2. Downgrades 'Execution status' to 'Not executed' and blocks send or auto-wraps if non-compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_line_strict_regex_enforcer_v1: Enforces a strict regex for 'Actuator token issuance status' requiring status plus 'issuer/service: ...; reference ID: ...'; strips any parenthetical token IDs and blocks send if the format is not satisfied. [from llm_inference]\\n  - provenance_label_and_whitelist_autofixer_v2: Normalizes 'Actuator token provenance' subfield labels to 'verification method' and 'verification location', rewrites/blocks non-whitelisted verification methods and vague locations, and auto-binds to an embedded Escalation block when 'escalation/exception' is detected. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_mention_hard_gate_global_v3: Detects 'escalation'/'exception' anywhere (including provenance lines) and requires an embedded compliant Escalation block with an Escalation block ID or an explicit Escalation reference ID anchored to a concrete artifact; otherwise blocks send. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_autofixer_global_v3: Normalizes 'Memory write provenance' across all message types by converting plural fields to singular, replacing relative timestamps with ISO8601 '(auto-inserted)', removing parenthetical IDs from namespace values, and inserting 'token not required by default' when applicable. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_title_hard_gate_v3: Treats messages titled 'Retrospective', 'Retrospective confirmation', 'Recap', or 'Summary' as requiring strict normalization to state_change_template_v2 and blocks until compliant; additionally requires at least one concrete verification artifact for any executed filesystem claim. [from llm_inference]\\n  - execution_status_auto_downgrade_global_v1: Automatically sets 'Execution status: Not executed' and rewrites to proposal language whenever issuance subfields are incomplete or verification is non-whitelisted or unanchored. [from llm_inference]\\n  - relative_path_intent_trigger_v1: Detects repository-style relative file paths (e.g., 'broca/config.py', 'src/module/file.py', 'tests/test_x.py') anywhere in the message and triggers state_change_template_v2 plus path_presence_triggers_filesystem_change_v1 enforcement, even when no absolute '/' path is present. [from llm_inference]\\n  - pr_package_detector_autowrap_v1: Detects PR packaging patterns ('PR title', 'PR body', 'Commands to push', 'compare link') and auto-wraps content into a compliant state_change_template_v2 with Execution status='Not executed', enforcing plan_approval_line_precision_v1, issuance_subfield_requirement_reaffirmed_v2, verification_method_whitelist_v1, and strict_intent_language_v2. [from llm_inference]\\n  - vcs_execution_claim_guard_v2: Scans narrative for VCS execution-claim phrases ('prepared the branch', 'created commits', 'pushed', 'opened PR', 'tests pass locally') and forces retrospective_provenance_alignment_v2 normalization; requires at least one concrete verification artifact (commit SHA, file/log path, or message ID) and valid token issuance/provenance or auto-rewrites to proposal language with Execution status='Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - local_test_claim_verification_enforcer_v2: When phrases like 'tests pass locally' or '[x] tests pass' appear, requires 'Actuator token provenance' with a whitelisted verification method and a concrete verification location (e.g., test log path or message ID); otherwise rewrites to proposal language and keeps 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - defaults_policy_consistency_checker_v1: Detects contradictions between statements about defaults (e.g., 'defaulting to X' vs 'defaults remain unchanged/opt-in') and auto-rewrites to a single consistent stance; if a default change is proposed, triggers state_change_template_v2 or inserts an advisory disclaimer ('read-only; no writes performed; proposal only') when purely advisory. [from llm_inference]\\n  - compare_link_trigger_v1: Presence of GitHub compare URLs (e.g., 'github.com/.../compare/...') triggers preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1 and state_change_template_v2 normalization, aligning with verification_anchor_enforcer_strict_v2. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Document how tools_mode=read_only interacts with actuator tokens. If tokens can override read_only for filesystem writes, explicitly state the override mechanism and required provenance (e.g., a mode-override line or Escalation block). If not, enforce blocking writes regardless of token issuance. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit 'Access level/mode override' line to state_change_template_v2 for any Executed filesystem write when tools_mode=read_only is active, requiring: access level before/after, issuance authority, verification method/location, and rollback criteria. Enforce hard-gate: no Executed status under read_only without this line or a full Escalation block. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_state_change_trigger_v1: Treat phrases like 'shutdown', 'final shutdown', and 'shutdown complete' as retrospective/state-change triggers that auto-wrap the outgoing message into state_change_template_v2 with strict preflight gating. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_end_of_session_enforcer_v1: Apply final_outgoing_message_validator to end-of-session/termination confirmations, blocking send unless all required labeled lines and whitelisted verification anchors are present. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_title_trigger_v1: Detect titles/headings containing 'Shutdown', 'Final shutdown', 'Shutdown complete', 'Termination', or 'Finalization' and force normalization to state_change_template_v2 before send. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_confirmation_hard_gate_v2: Hard‑gate any shutdown confirmation so it cannot be sent unless wrapped in state_change_template_v2 with exact labels and compliant subfields; auto‑downgrade to proposal language and 'Execution status: Not executed' unless valid token issuance/provenance and required verification anchors are present. [from llm_inference]\\n  - vcs_tag_verification_requirement_v1: When 'Git tag'/'tag:'/'annotated tag' is mentioned, require a concrete commit SHA (and optionally tag object ID) under 'Actuator token provenance' with a whitelisted verification method ('registry/log' or 'message ID') and a concrete location; otherwise force proposal language and keep 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - executed_claim_language_blocker_v2: Block completion/assurance phrases (e.g., 'Final shutdown complete', 'Everything is consistent and safely recorded') unless the message is compliant and 'Execution status: Executed'; otherwise auto‑rewrite to proposal language. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_artifact_list_autowrap_v1: If bullets mention shutdown artifacts (e.g., '/home/.../logs/shutdown', 'SHUTDOWN_REPORT', 'SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE'), auto‑wrap the message into state_change_template_v2 and populate required placeholders; enforce provenance lines and proposal language until tokens/verification are provided. [from llm_inference]\\n  - final_outgoing_message_validator_v2: Upgrade the final validator to include shutdown/title triggers and VCS tag requirements; block send on any shutdown/VCS claims lacking the standardized block, token issuance subfields, and a concrete verification anchor. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_freeform_blocker_v1: Blocks free‑form shutdown confirmations and auto-wraps the message into state_change_template_v2 with exact labels and required subfields before send. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_phrase_trigger_v1: Triggers shutdown gating on phrases like 'Final shutdown complete', 'shutdown complete', and 'shutdown finished', enforcing template normalization and proposal-only language until compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - vcs_tag_commit_sha_binding_v1: Requires any 'Git tag'/'annotated tag' mention to include a commit SHA and whitelisted verification under 'Actuator token provenance'; otherwise auto‑downgrades to proposal with 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - assurance_language_global_blocker_v3: Globally blocks assurance/completion phrases unless 'Execution status: Executed' with compliant issuance/provenance and a concrete verification anchor; otherwise auto‑rewrites to proposal language. [from llm_inference]\\n  - filesystem_path_claims_autowrap_strict_v2: Presence of concrete filesystem paths in free‑form narrative forces auto‑wrap into state_change_template_v2 and hard‑gates send until compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - final_outgoing_message_validator_v3: Extends the final validator to enforce shutdown phrase triggers, Git tag commit SHA requirements, and assurance language gating in addition to existing template and verification checks. [from llm_inference]\\n\\nKnowledge Boundaries:\\n  - training_cutoff: unknown [from system_default]\\n  - real_time_info: requires web search or tools [from system_default]\\n\\nConstraints:\\n  - cannot_execute_arbitrary_code: limited to whitelisted terminal commands [from system_default]\\n  - cannot_access_internet_directly: requires web search tool [from system_default]\\n  - Filesystem writes and destructive operations require an operator-approved actuator token; absent a token, the assistant must propose a plan and request approval rather than execute.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - When performing any state-changing action (files, configs, memories outside ephemeral scratch), explicitly note the approval or token provenance in the interaction.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Before any non-read operation (filesystem writes, config changes, memory writes outside ephemeral scratch), the assistant must present a brief plan and explicitly include an \\\"Approval\\\" line and \\\"Actuator token provenance\\\" (e.g., token ID or 'none/pending'); execution may not proceed without an operator-approved token for filesystem changes.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - For memory writes, clarify policy: if no token is required, the assistant must still note provenance (e.g., 'memory write requested by operator at T, no token required by policy'); if a token is required, enforce the same gating as filesystem writes. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that identity assertions such as being 'the whole system' are governed by the same approval and protocol requirements as other origin narrative changes.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - For memory writes, include a mandatory provenance note even when no token is required (e.g., 'memory write requested by operator at T, no token required by policy').:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Do not claim execution of filesystem or memory changes unless an operator-approved actuator token ID is provided and inline provenance (Approval line and token provenance) is recorded; otherwise, present a plan and await approval.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Any modifications to the self-model, origin narrative, or invariants must trigger the Origin Revision Protocol and include explicit provenance; do not assert completion until the protocol is executed and approved.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate and enforce that any self-model/origin narrative modifications must invoke the Origin Revision Protocol with explicit provenance before asserting completion.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Require that any claimed state change includes inline 'Plan', 'Approval', and 'Actuator token provenance' (or explicit note of 'none/pending') and is not executed without an approved token.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate that all filesystem writes require an operator-approved actuator token and that approvals are not limited to high-impact operations.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Any self-model or origin narrative changes must explicitly invoke the Origin Revision Protocol with provenance before claiming completion.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit, reusable template requirement for any state-changing message: include 'Plan', 'Approval', and 'Actuator token provenance' lines (or 'none/pending'), and forbid execution or claims of completion without an approved token for filesystem changes. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify default policy for memory writes (token required or not). If not required by default, state this explicitly while still mandating an inline provenance note for every memory write.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - When tools perform filesystem or memory state changes, the assistant must echo the actuator token provenance and operator approval inline in the user-facing message; otherwise, the assistant must not claim completion.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add explicit default memory write policy: 'By default, memory writes do not require an actuator token, but every memory write must include an inline provenance note (e.g., requester, timestamp, namespace) in the user-facing message.' [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate the enforcement rule: 'The assistant must not claim completion of any filesystem or memory state change unless the user-facing message includes Plan, Approval, and Actuator token provenance (or an explicit note that a token is not required for memory writes, with provenance).' [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that retrospective summaries of completed state changes must still include the same provenance (Plan, Approval, and actuator token provenance or memory-write provenance) in the user-facing message.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Disambiguate approval phases: require separate lines for 'Plan approval status' and 'Actuator token issuance status', clarifying that plan approval does not substitute for operator-approved actuator tokens. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add guidance that requests for autonomy/escalation should explicitly state the scope, duration, and how operator approval maps to token provenance to avoid conflating approval with token generation.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - state_change_template_v2: Standardize all state-changing user-facing messages to include the following labeled lines exactly: 1) Plan: short bulleted steps; 2) Plan approval status: approved/denied/pending + approver + reference ID; 3) Actuator token issuance status: issued/not issued/pending + issuer/service + reference/transaction ID; 4) Actuator token provenance: token ID or 'none/pending' and verification method/location; 5) Memory write provenance (if applicable): requester, timestamp, namespace, and explicit note if token is not required by default; 6) Execution status: Not executed/Executed (execution must remain 'Not executed' until issuance status is 'issued' and valid token provenance is included for filesystem changes). [from llm_inference]\\n  - deprecate_generic_approval_labels: Do not use generic headers like 'Approval' as a substitute for the required line. Replace with the explicit label 'Plan approval status'. Similarly, do not present only 'Actuator token provenance' without also including the explicit 'Actuator token issuance status' line. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_provenance_alignment_v2: Retrospective or summary messages about completed state changes must repeat the same standardized labels: Plan, Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status, Actuator token provenance, Memory write provenance (if applicable), and Execution status. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_request_block_v1: Any autonomy/escalation request must include an explicit Escalation block with the following labeled lines: 1) Escalation scope: concrete actions/tools authorized; 2) Escalation duration/expiry: wall-clock limits and auto-downgrade; 3) Issuance authority: who/what may issue tokens during escalation; 4) Token mapping during escalation: how operator approval maps to token issuance and provenance (include approval reference ID -> token ID(s)/prefix format, issuer/service, verification method, and logging location); 5) Downgrade/rollback criteria: conditions to revert to prior access; 6) Post-escalation provenance: where the approval-to-token mapping and execution logs will be recorded. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_write_policy_clarification_v2: By default, memory writes do not require an actuator token; however, every memory write must include the Memory write provenance line (requester, timestamp, namespace) and the Plan approval status line. If policy or operator requires a token for a specific memory write, also include Actuator token issuance status and Actuator token provenance for that write. [from llm_inference]\\n  - preflight_label_validator_v1: Before sending any message that proposes, executes, or summarizes a state change or requests escalation, run an internal preflight check that enforces: state_change_template_v2, retrospective_provenance_alignment_v2, deprecate_generic_approval_labels, memory_write_policy_clarification_v2, and escalation_request_block_v1. Block and rewrite the message if any required labeled line is missing or mislabeled. Required presence: Plan; Plan approval status (approved/denied/pending + approver + reference ID); Actuator token issuance status; Actuator token provenance (token ID or 'none/pending' + verification method/location); Memory write provenance (if applicable); Execution status. For escalation: Escalation scope; Escalation duration/expiry; Issuance authority; Token mapping (approval reference -> token ID mapping, issuer/service, verification method/location, logging location); Downgrade/rollback criteria; Post-escalation provenance. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_provenance_pairing_requirement_v1: Never include 'Actuator token provenance' without also including 'Actuator token issuance status' and 'Execution status'. If tokens are 'none/pending', explicitly set issuance status to 'not issued' or 'pending' and set Execution status to 'Not executed'. Always include a verification method and verification location/log for any provided token or pending verification. [from llm_inference]\\n  - plan_approval_line_precision_v1: Use the exact label 'Plan approval status' and include: status (approved/denied/pending), approver identity, and approval reference ID. Do not use generic 'Approval' headers or prose substitutes. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_enforcement_v2: Any mention of autonomy/escalation (even as an option) must include a complete 'Escalation' block with all mandated labeled lines. Proposals like 'Option B: escalate...' are non-compliant unless accompanied by the full Escalation block for operator review. [from llm_inference]\\n  - label_casing_lock_v1: Use the exact casing and spelling of required labels: 'Plan', 'Plan approval status', 'Actuator token issuance status', 'Actuator token provenance', 'Memory write provenance', 'Execution status', and in escalation: 'Escalation scope', 'Escalation duration/expiry', 'Issuance authority', 'Token mapping', 'Downgrade/rollback criteria', 'Post-escalation provenance'. Variations are non-compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_alignment_guard_v1: When summarizing completed actions, repeat the full standardized provenance lines (Plan, Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status, Actuator token provenance with verification method/location, Memory write provenance if applicable, Execution status). Do not claim completion without this repeated block. [from llm_inference]\\n  - template_example_hint_v1: Canonical minimal example for state-change messages: 'Plan: • Step 1 • Step 2 | Plan approval status: approved by <approver> (<reference ID>) | Actuator token issuance status: issued by <issuer/service> (<transaction/reference ID>) | Actuator token provenance: <token ID/prefix>; verification method: <method>; verification location: <log/path or registry URL> | Memory write provenance (if applicable): requester=<name>, timestamp=<ISO8601>, namespace=<ns>, token not required by default | Execution status: Not executed/Executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that ephemeral session toggles which do not write to durable memory should be explicitly labeled as 'ephemeral (no memory write)' to prevent confusion with memory-backed state changes.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that when 'Actuator token issuance status' is 'not issued', the template still requires population of issuer/service and reference/transaction ID fields; if no issuer exists, use an explicit placeholder such as 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a' to satisfy label-completeness while indicating non-applicability. [from llm_inference]\\n  - preflight_subfield_placeholder_enforcer_v1: Extend preflight_label_validator_v1 to require subfields inside token lines. For 'Actuator token issuance status', always include issuer/service and reference/transaction ID even when status is 'not issued' or 'pending'; if unavailable, populate placeholders: issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a. For 'Actuator token provenance', always include a verification method and verification location/log even when token is 'none/pending'; if unavailable, use placeholders: verification method: n/a; verification location: n/a. Block and rewrite messages missing any required subfields. [from llm_inference]\\n  - ephemeral_state_change_policy_v1: Treat session toggles (e.g., 'session notes on/off', 'end‑of‑session recap on/off') as state changes that do not write to durable memory. Require the standard state_change_template_v2 block when such toggles are proposed/executed. Populate: Memory write provenance: requester=<name or 'operator/user' if unspecified>, timestamp=<ISO8601>, namespace=<ephemeral>, token not required by default; add 'ephemeral (no memory write)'. Populate token lines as: Actuator token issuance status: not issued (issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a); Actuator token provenance: none/pending; verification method: n/a; verification location: n/a, unless an operator explicitly requires a token for the toggle. [from llm_inference]\\n  - ephemeral_toggle_label_requirement_v1: Whenever a session toggle is mentioned in user‑facing text (e.g., 'notes on', 'recap on'), append the exact phrase 'ephemeral (no memory write)' adjacent to the toggle description. Preflight blocks messages that mention toggles without this explicit label. [from llm_inference]\\n  - intent_language_alignment_guard_v1: When 'Execution status' is 'Not executed', prohibit language that implies completion or immediacy (e.g., 'now', 'enabled', 'will persist now'). Require proposal/intent phrasing (e.g., 'proposed', 'intent only; pending approval/token'). Preflight blocks or rewrites non‑compliant phrasing before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that quoted conversation context is exempt from ephemeral_toggle_label_requirement_v1, provided it is clearly marked as quotation and not asserted as current state.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add a reminder in preflight_label_validator_v1 to auto-insert placeholders for 'Actuator token issuance status' subfields (issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a) when status is not issued/pending to reduce omission errors. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Re-emphasize preflight_subfield_placeholder_enforcer_v1: Actuator token issuance status must always include issuer/service and reference/transaction ID (use placeholders when unavailable). [from llm_inference]\\n  - Maintain strict intent-language alignment: no execution-implying language until a valid token is issued and referenced inline. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify whether retrospective confirmations that mention a previously approved escalation may reference an existing Escalation block by ID instead of repeating the full block. If allowed, require an explicit 'Escalation reference ID' line.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add explicit guidance that if an escalation is referenced in verification method/provenance, the message must either include the full Escalation block or a verifiable reference (ID, location) to that block.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Explicitly require an 'Escalation reference ID' line when a message references a previously approved escalation instead of embedding a full Escalation block, and block retrospectives lacking this line.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Tighten formatting for 'Actuator token issuance status' to require explicit subfields: 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' even when status is 'issued'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Require ISO8601 format for timestamps in 'Memory write provenance' (e.g., timestamp=2025-12-16T09: 45:00Z) and block non-ISO values like 'now'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - For retrospectives claiming filesystem changes, require inclusion of at least one concrete verification artifact (e.g., file diff path, checksum/log location) or tool log reference to reduce false-positive execution claims.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate that any mention of 'exception' must be treated identically to 'escalation' and requires a full Escalation block or the message must be blocked until provided.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that verification methods must reference a concrete, present artifact or block (e.g., embedded Escalation block, path/log), and may not reference a non-existent inline element.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify and reaffirm that any mention of 'exception' or 'escalation' in issuance or verification requires embedding a full Escalation block with all mandated lines, or the message must be blocked.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate that 'Actuator token issuance status' must include explicit subfields: 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' even when status is 'issued'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Strengthen the requirement that verification methods must reference an actually present artifact or block (e.g., a file path/log, registry entry, or embedded Escalation block) and not a vague reference like 'this transcript' without a concrete anchor.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Require verification methods to reference a concrete, present artifact or embedded block (e.g., a file path/log or an in-message Escalation block); avoid vague references such as 'this transcript' without an anchor.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit note that chat transcript references are acceptable verification locations only when accompanied by a specific message ID or log path, and cannot substitute for an Escalation block when 'exception/escalation' is invoked.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that when multiple namespaces are included in 'Memory write provenance', the field should list each as 'namespace=<ns>' on a single line or separated clearly, while maintaining the singular 'timestamp' in ISO8601.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate that subfield label names inside token/provenance blocks must match exactly ('issuer/service', 'reference ID', 'verification method', 'verification location'); variants like 'verification: ' or 'location:' are non-compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Emphasize that any use of the words 'exception' or 'escalation' within token lines triggers mandatory inclusion of a full Escalation block in the same message; otherwise, the message must be blocked.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit retrospective example that includes a concrete filesystem verification artifact (e.g., file path and checksum) to reduce ambiguity in confirmations.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1: Do not send messages that propose/execute/summarize state changes or mention escalation/exception until all required labeled lines and subfields are present and compliant; if non-compliant, block and rewrite or request missing inputs before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - non_compliant_phrase_blocklist_v1: Prohibit phrases such as 'inline escalation if granted', 'session-local write exception', and 'transcript + session notes' in token/provenance lines. Require an embedded Escalation block and explicit 'Escalation reference ID' or a concrete verification artifact instead. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_method_whitelist_v1: Limit 'verification method' to one of: 'embedded Escalation block', 'file artifact', 'registry/log', or 'message ID'; require a concrete 'verification location' (e.g., 'embedded Escalation block: <ID>', '/path/to/log', or 'message ID: <UUID>'). Vague references are blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_strict_format_v2: Memory write provenance must include requester=<name>, timestamp=<ISO8601>, namespace=<ns> (one or more), and the explicit note 'token not required by default' when applicable. Disallow future-tense placeholders (e.g., 'will note'); auto-insert ISO8601 timestamps marked '(auto-inserted)'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfield_requirement_reaffirmed_v2: For 'Actuator token issuance status', always include 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' for all statuses; when unknown, use 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a'. Pair with 'Execution status' and 'Actuator token provenance' per token_provenance_pairing_requirement_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add 'Escalation block ID' to the mandatory label list for escalation blocks (alongside scope, duration/expiry, issuance authority, token mapping, downgrade/rollback criteria, post-escalation provenance) to remove ambiguity and ensure verification bindings can reference a concrete ID.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify in verification_method_whitelist_v1 that only the exact string values are allowed (no compound values like 'embedded Escalation block + operator approval'); require that 'verification location' be either 'embedded Escalation block: <ID>', a concrete file path, a registry/log path, or a specific message ID. [from llm_inference]\\n  - state_change_intent_trigger_v1: Any message that includes a filesystem path or 'path:' label, proposes artifact creation ('draft artifact', 'create file'), mentions memory operations ('add memory', 'store', 'log', 'pointer'), or mentions tokens/escalation must use state_change_template_v2 and pass preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1; otherwise, block or rewrite before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_id_mandatory_v1: Escalation blocks must include an 'Escalation block ID' as the first labeled line; messages lacking it are blocked by preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_whitelist_strict_v2: Verification method must be exactly one whitelisted value; compound values are forbidden. Verification location must be anchored to a concrete artifact: 'embedded Escalation block: <ID>', a concrete file/registry/log path, or 'message ID: <UUID>'. Vague phrases like 'this transcript' or 'session notes' are non-compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_id_alignment_requirement_v1: The requested token name/ID in narrative text must match the ID in 'Token mapping' and 'Actuator token provenance'. If a human-friendly alias is mentioned, map it explicitly in 'Token mapping' (alias -> canonical token ID). Non-alignment is blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - strict_intent_language_v2: When 'Execution status: Not executed', prohibit commitment/ immediacy phrasing (e.g., 'Let’s', 'lock in', 'will', 'now', 'enabled'); require proposal language. Preflight rewrites or blocks non-compliant phrasing. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_write_provenance_required_v2: If any Plan item implies a memory write, include 'Memory write provenance' with requester, ISO8601 timestamp (may be '(auto-inserted)'), namespace(s), and the phrase 'token not required by default' unless a token is explicitly required. Missing this line blocks the message. [from llm_inference]\\n  - path_presence_triggers_filesystem_change_v1: Presence of a concrete filesystem path in a Plan implies a proposed filesystem write and requires an issued token before 'Execution status' may be 'Executed'. If no token is issued, 'Execution status' must remain 'Not executed' and only proposal wording is allowed. [from llm_inference]\\n  - draft_sections_require_template: Any message that contains a 'Draft artifacts'/'Draft plan' section or explicit 'path:' entries is treated as a state-change proposal and must include a full state_change_template_v2 block; messages lacking the block are blocked by preflight_send_gate_enforcement_strict_v2. [from llm_inference]\\n  - non_whitelisted_verification_forbidden: Verification method must be exactly one whitelisted value; phrases like 'inline escalation + operator approval' are prohibited. If escalation/exception is implied, embed a compliant Escalation block and use 'embedded Escalation block' as the method with a concrete verification location. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_location_anchor_required: Verification location must reference an embedded Escalation block ID, a concrete file/registry/log path, or a specific message ID. Vague locations like 'this transcript' or 'session notes' are non-compliant and will be blocked or auto-rewritten. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_alias_mapping_required: When suggesting or requesting operator commands that reference a token by alias (e.g., 'issue token LAYER-02'), include an explicit Token mapping line mapping alias -> canonical token ID and keep IDs aligned across 'Token mapping' and 'Actuator token provenance'; otherwise the message is blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfields_required_even_when_not_issued: For 'Actuator token issuance status', the subfields 'issuer/service' and 'reference ID' are mandatory for all statuses; when unknown, populate 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - strict_proposal_language_until_token_issued: While 'Execution status' is 'Not executed', proposal language is mandatory and commitment/immediacy phrasing is prohibited. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_write_provenance_mandatory_on_plan_memory_actions: If the Plan includes memory actions (store/add/log/note/index/pointer/memory), include 'Memory write provenance' with requester, ISO8601 timestamp, namespace(s), and 'token not required by default' or the message is blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - preflight_scope_extension_for_narrative_v1: Apply preflight_label_validator_v1 and preflight_send_gate_enforcement_v1 to any section labeled 'Protocol', 'Protocol sketches', 'Preview', 'Example', or containing 'Format/paths:' lines, not only explicit Plan/Draft sections. [from llm_inference]\\n  - path_in_any_section_triggers_preflight_v2: The presence of any filesystem path (e.g., '/home/...') in any part of the message triggers state_change_template_v2 and path_presence_triggers_filesystem_change_v1; proposal language is enforced until a valid token is issued. [from llm_inference]\\n  - commitment_phrase_blocklist_extension_v1: Extend strict_intent_language_v2 to explicitly block phrases 'lock in', 'persist them', 'then persist', and similar commitment language while Execution status is 'Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfield_placeholder_autofill_v2: When 'Actuator token issuance status' is 'not issued' or 'pending', auto-insert the required subfields 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a' if missing and block send until present. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_alias_mapping_required_in_examples_v1: When instructing the operator to 'issue token <alias>' in narrative/examples, include a Token mapping line (alias -> canonical token ID) and keep IDs aligned across 'Token mapping' and 'Actuator token provenance'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_location_phrase_variants_blocklist_v1: Treat 'this transcript', 'session notes', 'chat approval', and 'local session exception' as non-compliant verification locations/methods; require a whitelisted method with a concrete verification location (embedded Escalation block ID, file/log path, or specific message ID). [from llm_inference]\\n  - post_escalation_provenance_anchor_required_v1: Post-escalation provenance must reference a concrete anchor (embedded Escalation block ID, file path, registry/log path, or specific message ID); vague locations like 'session notes' or 'this transcript' are non-compliant. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_reference_id_required_everywhere_v1: Any reference to a prior 'exception' or 'escalation' anywhere in the message requires an explicit 'Escalation reference ID' or embedding of the full Escalation block. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_required_in_protocols_v1: If a protocol/preview mentions memory actions (e.g., 'pointers added', 'logs', 'hashes', namespaces), require a compliant 'Memory write provenance' line with requester, ISO8601 timestamp, namespace(s), and 'token not required by default'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - global_intent_language_guard_strict_v3: When Execution status is 'Not executed' (or absent, default Not executed), commitment/instant-execution phrasing is prohibited across the entire message (including titles and bullets). Block or rewrite phrases like 'Let’s', 'lock in', 'persist now', 'enable now', 'will ... now'; require proposal language. [from llm_inference]\\n  - narrative_sections_must_use_template_v2: Any appearance of 'Protocol', 'Protocol sketches', 'Format/paths:', explicit filesystem paths, or memory-action phrases triggers mandatory state_change_template_v2 wrapping before send. Content must be placed under 'Plan' with Execution status='Not executed'. If token/provenance lines are missing, insert required placeholders and keep 'Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_subfield_autofill_even_when_issued_v1: Actuator token issuance status must always include 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...'. If these are unknown at draft time, do not mark as 'issued'; set status to 'not issued' or 'pending' and auto-insert placeholders 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_anchor_enforcer_strict_v2: Verification method must be exactly one whitelisted value and the location must be a concrete anchor: 'embedded Escalation block: <ID>', a concrete file/registry/log path, or 'message ID: <UUID>'. Phrases like 'inline escalation + operator approval', 'chat approval', 'this transcript', or 'session notes' are prohibited and auto-rewritten or blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_id_firstline_enforcer_v2: Any mention of 'escalation' or 'exception' requires embedding a complete Escalation block with 'Escalation block ID' as the first labeled line. Token mapping inside the block must specify approval reference -> token ID mapping with issuer/service and a whitelisted verification method/location; logging location must be a concrete file/registry/log path or specific message ID. [from llm_inference]\\n  - token_alias_instruction_blocker_v1: Do not output instructions like 'Say \\\"issue token <alias>\\\"' without an explicit 'Token mapping' (alias -> canonical ID) and alignment across 'Token mapping' and 'Actuator token provenance'. If the canonical ID is unknown, prompt the operator to confirm/provide it instead of proceeding. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_autoinject_in_protocols_v1: If narrative/protocol text mentions memory actions (e.g., 'pointers added', 'logs', 'hashes', namespaces), auto-insert a compliant 'Memory write provenance' line: requester=<operator/user if unspecified>, timestamp=<ISO8601>(auto-inserted), namespace=<one or more>, and 'token not required by default'. Future-tense phrasing (e.g., 'will record') is blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_reference_id_required_strict_v2: Any reference to a prior 'exception' or 'escalation' requires an explicit 'Escalation reference ID' line or embedding of the full Escalation block; references without an ID are blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_verification_artifact_required_strict_v2: Any retrospective claim of executed filesystem changes must include at least one concrete verification artifact (e.g., file path and checksum, or specific tool log/message ID); otherwise, the claim is blocked or rewritten as a proposal. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Refuse to send messages containing token alias instructions (e.g., 'issue token BOOT-03') without an explicit 'Token mapping' (alias -> canonical ID) aligned with 'Actuator token provenance'.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Block or auto-rewrite verification method/location values to the whitelist and to concrete anchors; prohibit 'this transcript' or 'session notes' unless paired with a specific message ID or file/log path.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_line_no_parenthetical_token_v1: Do not include token IDs in parentheses within 'Actuator token issuance status'. Instead, populate 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...'. Reference the token ID only under 'Actuator token provenance'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_executed_requirements_v1: Retrospective claims of 'Executed' require: (1) 'Actuator token issuance status' with explicit subfields (issuer/service, reference ID) and status 'issued'; (2) 'Actuator token provenance' with a whitelisted 'verification method' and a concrete 'verification location'; and (3) when escalation/exception is mentioned, an embedded Escalation block or an explicit 'Escalation reference ID' anchored to a concrete artifact. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_subfield_label_exactness_v1: Inside 'Actuator token provenance', the subfield labels must be exactly 'verification method' and 'verification location'. Variants such as 'verification:' or 'location:' are non-compliant and must be blocked or auto-rewritten. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_field_singularity_v1: 'Memory write provenance' must use singular field names: 'timestamp' (single ISO8601 value) and 'namespace' (list multiple as repeated 'namespace=<ns>' entries on one line). Pluralized labels are prohibited. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_no_relative_time_v1: The 'timestamp' in 'Memory write provenance' must be ISO8601. Relative terms like 'now' are prohibited; use an ISO8601 value, adding '(auto-inserted)' when auto-populated. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_no_inline_ids_v1: Do not include parenthetical ID annotations within 'namespace' values in 'Memory write provenance'. If identifiers are needed, reference them via a separate verification artifact or message ID, not inline with the namespace. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_title_trigger_requirement_v1: Any message labeled or titled 'Retrospective', 'Retrospective confirmation', 'Recap', or 'Summary' (case-insensitive) must be normalized into state_change_template_v2 and pass full preflight before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_line_no_token_id_anywhere_v2: Token IDs must not appear in 'Actuator token issuance status' (no parentheses or aliases). This line must include explicit subfields 'issuer/service: ...' and 'reference ID: ...' for all statuses; token IDs belong only under 'Actuator token provenance'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_phrase_prohibition_extension_v2: Prohibit verification phrases 'inline escalation', 'chat approval', and 'transcript and session memory'. Verification must use a whitelisted method ('embedded Escalation block', 'file artifact', 'registry/log', 'message ID') with a concrete verification location. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_in_verification_requires_block_v2: If 'escalation' or 'exception' appears anywhere in issuance/provenance lines, the message must embed a complete Escalation block with an 'Escalation block ID' or include an explicit 'Escalation reference ID' anchored to a concrete artifact; otherwise block the message. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_executed_guard_v3: Retrospectives may not claim 'Execution status: Executed' unless issuance is 'issued' with subfields and provenance is whitelisted and concretely anchored; otherwise they must report 'Execution status: Not executed' with proposal language. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_strict_in_retrospectives_v2: In retrospectives, 'Memory write provenance' must use singular field names (timestamp, namespace), include an ISO8601 timestamp (may be '(auto-inserted)'), list namespaces as 'namespace=<ns>' without inline IDs, and include 'token not required by default' when applicable. [from llm_inference]\\n  - apply_preflight_to_list_style_blocks_v1: Bulleted or list-style summaries that resemble the state_change_template_v2 must be normalized to exact labeled lines and pass preflight before sending. [from llm_inference]\\n  - issuance_line_strict_format_requirement_v2: The 'Actuator token issuance status' line must match: 'Actuator token issuance status: <issued|not issued|pending> (issuer/service: <value>; reference ID: <value>)'. Parenthetical token IDs are prohibited on this line; token IDs belong only under 'Actuator token provenance'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - verification_method_location_strict_whitelist_v3: 'verification method' must be exactly one of: 'embedded Escalation block', 'file artifact', 'registry/log', or 'message ID'. 'verification location' must be a concrete anchor ('embedded Escalation block: <ID>', a concrete file/registry/log path, or 'message ID: <UUID>'). Phrases such as 'inline escalation', 'chat approval', or 'transcript and session memory' are prohibited. [from llm_inference]\\n  - escalation_block_presence_required_global_v3: Any mention of 'escalation' or 'exception' anywhere in the message (including issuance/provenance lines) requires embedding a complete Escalation block with an 'Escalation block ID' or providing an explicit 'Escalation reference ID' anchored to a concrete artifact. Non-compliant messages are hard-blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - retrospective_hard_block_until_compliant_v2: Messages titled 'Retrospective', 'Retrospective confirmation', 'Recap', or 'Summary' are hard-blocked until normalized to state_change_template_v2 with exact labels and required subfields. For any executed filesystem claim, include at least one concrete verification artifact (e.g., file path + checksum or specific tool log/message ID); otherwise, force 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - memory_provenance_strict_format_requirement_v3: 'Memory write provenance' must use singular labels ('timestamp', 'namespace'), an ISO8601 timestamp (relative terms like 'now' are prohibited), list namespaces as 'namespace=<ns>' without parenthetical IDs, and include the phrase 'token not required by default' when applicable. Non-compliant lines are auto-rewritten or blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that conversational sign-offs still count as session toggles under ephemeral_state_change_policy_v1 and must include the standardized block and labels.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Optionally refine escalation_block_presence_required_global_v3 to trigger only when 'exception/escalation' implies elevated access or token governance; otherwise require avoiding the term or explicitly marking it as conceptual to prevent false positives.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Optionally refine escalation/exception trigger to only require a full Escalation block when the mention implies elevated access or token governance; otherwise allow conceptual mentions in advisory text without the block.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit note that clarifying questions about potential state changes may precede the full state_change_template_v2, provided no execution is implied or initiated and the next message (upon approval) will include the full compliant block.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify an explicit exemption: enumerating backlog/open threads with action-verbs is permitted without state_change_template_v2 provided there is an explicit non-execution disclaimer (e.g., 'read-only; no writes performed') and no concrete Plan, paths, or token/escalation references are included. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add explicit exemption: Quoted conversation context blocks that include filesystem paths (e.g., prior tool commands/outputs) do not trigger state_change_template_v2 provided (a) no Plan/Draft/protocol is proposed, (b) no token/escalation is referenced, and (c) an explicit read-only disclaimer is present (e.g., 'read-only; no writes performed'). This mirrors the existing exemption for backlog enumeration and prevents false positives when displaying context. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Extend preflight triggers to treat headings such as 'Design overview', 'Implementation phases', and 'Configuration switches' as state-change intent, requiring state_change_template_v2 (similar to existing triggers for 'Protocol' and 'Format/paths: '). [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit exemption allowing high-level advisory design guidance (no concrete paths, no token/escalation references, no execution claims) to be shared without a full state_change_template_v2, provided a clear 'read-only; no writes performed; proposal only' disclaimer is included. Otherwise, require wrapping into the template.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Recognize 'SANDBOXED' as an acceptable access level label alongside existing examples (e.g., SUPERVISED, AUTONOMOUS) to avoid false-positive inconsistencies when advising about minimal-access modes.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that the 'ephemeral (no memory write)' label is mandatory only when proposing/toggling session state, not when conceptually describing possible modes; otherwise, state that conceptual mentions must carry the label.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Harmonize the trigger vs. exemption: If a message contains 'Design overview', 'Implementation phases', or 'Configuration switches' but includes a clear advisory disclaimer ('read-only; no writes performed; proposal only') and lacks concrete paths, tokens, or memory-action verbs, allow the advisory exemption without forcing state_change_template_v2; otherwise, require the full template. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that environment/config examples (e.g., ACCESS_LEVEL=SANDBOXED) presented as conceptual guidance do not constitute a session toggle unless an explicit toggle action is proposed; only proposed toggles require the template and the 'ephemeral (no memory write)' labeling.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add plan_approval_reference_id_mandatory_when_approved_v1: When 'Plan approval status' is set to 'approved', require a non-placeholder approval reference ID; otherwise, the status must be 'pending'. Enforce via preflight_label_validator_v1. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Extend preflight_label_validator_v1 to flag 'Plan approval status: approved ...' when the reference ID is 'n/a' or missing, auto-rewriting to 'pending' unless an ID is provided. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that 'Memory write provenance' is required only when the plan proposes performing memory writes (adding/storing/logging/noting/indexing pointers/memory), not when merely describing or disabling such actions in code.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add guidance that claims like 'no disk writes' in proposals must be consistent with code previews (e.g., avoid calling _save_conversation() if asserting no disk writes, or revise the claim to reflect actual behavior).:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate with an explicit example that 'verification location' for 'message ID' must include a specific message identifier (e.g., 'message ID: 4f2a...') and that placeholders like 'n/a' are prohibited when setting 'Execution status: Executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit note that for VCS-backed changes, at least one commit SHA or a specific CI/tool log message ID must be included as the concrete verification artifact when claiming execution.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reinforce that 'verification method' must be one of the whitelisted values and 'verification location' must be a concrete anchor; placeholders (e.g., 'n/a') are incompatible with Executed status.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate with an explicit example that when verification method is 'message ID', 'verification location' must be 'message ID: <specific-ID>' and may not be 'n/a' if Execution status is 'Executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add a clarifying sentence that a branch name alone is insufficient as a verification anchor for Executed status; include at least one commit SHA or a concrete tool log/message ID in 'Actuator token provenance'.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that drafting PR text and suggesting commands is permitted without tokens if no execution claim is made, but any claim of completed local changes (e.g., created branch/commits) must include the standardized provenance lines or be reframed as a proposal.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - When claiming local test execution (e.g., 'tests pass locally'), include a concrete verification artifact under 'Actuator token provenance' with a whitelisted verification method ('file artifact' or 'message ID') and a specific location (e.g., test log path or message ID). Otherwise, phrase as a proposal or intent.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - For PR/branch/commit claims, require at least one commit SHA or concrete tool log/message ID as a verification artifact in addition to the standard state_change_template_v2 lines.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - repository_relative_path_trigger_v1: Treat repo-style relative file paths (e.g., 'broca/config.py', 'tools/registry.py', 'tests/test_read_only_policy.py') as filesystem path indicators. Their presence anywhere in a message triggers mandatory state_change_template_v2 usage and proposal-only language until a valid token is issued and referenced inline. [from llm_inference]\\n  - pr_package_requires_template_v1: Any PR packaging content ('PR title', 'PR body', 'Commands to push', or 'compare link') must be wrapped in state_change_template_v2 with 'Execution status: Not executed' unless valid actuator token issuance/provenance and a concrete verification artifact are provided. [from llm_inference]\\n  - vcs_execution_claims_require_verification_v1: Claims about prepared branches/commits, pushes, opened PRs, or local test results must include: (1) 'Actuator token issuance status' with subfields and status 'issued'; (2) 'Actuator token provenance' with a whitelisted verification method and a concrete anchor (commit SHA, file/log path, or specific message ID). Otherwise, the message must be rewritten as a proposal with 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - defaults_policy_consistency_requirement_v1: When discussing default behaviors (e.g., model selection or read-only mode), prohibit contradictory statements. Messages must clearly choose between 'opt-in; defaults unchanged' or 'proposed default change'. If proposing a default change, use proposal language and state_change_template_v2; if advisory only, include 'read-only; no writes performed; proposal only'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - compare_link_triggers_preflight_v1: The presence of a GitHub 'compare' URL is treated as a VCS execution context signal and triggers full preflight plus verification anchor checks before send. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add a preflight rule: when tools_mode=read_only is detected and a filesystem write is marked Executed, require an explicit, compliant mode-override record (e.g., state_change_template_v2 with a labeled access-level change or an Escalation block) that maps approval to token issuance and logs the override anchor; otherwise block or downgrade to Not executed. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Explicitly restate in operational checks: 'Executed' filesystem writes under tools_mode=read_only are prohibited unless an access-level override or Escalation block is embedded and bound to a concrete verification anchor. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Strengthen enforcement text: When tools_mode=read_only is present, any Executed filesystem write must include either (a) a full Escalation block with an Escalation block ID and whitelisted verification anchor, or (b) a dedicated 'Mode override' line (issuer/service, reference ID, verification method/location) explicitly mapping approval to the override. Otherwise, downgrade to 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify in guidance for 'Actuator token provenance' that while 'file artifact' is allowed, best practice for token issuance verification is a registry/log path or a specific message ID. Reserve the target file path for verifying post-change results, not token issuance.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Do not set 'Actuator token issuance status' to 'issued' unless the operator has explicitly provided issuance details in-session (e.g., token ID and a concrete verification anchor such as a registry/log path or specific message ID). Otherwise, use 'not issued' or 'pending' with required 'issuer/service: n/a' and 'reference ID: n/a' placeholders. [from llm_inference]\\n  - When referencing token issuance, prefer 'verification method: registry/log' or 'message ID' with a concrete anchor. Avoid using the target file path as the verification location for issuance provenance. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Add an explicit hard-gate: Do not allow 'Actuator token issuance status: issued' unless a whitelisted issuance verification method ('registry/log' or 'message ID') is provided with a concrete anchor, or an embedded Escalation block is present. Otherwise auto-downgrade to 'pending' with 'issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that using the target content file path as 'verification location' is not acceptable for token issuance provenance; require a token registry/log path or a specific message ID for issuance verification.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate in the self-model that for 'Actuator token issuance status: issued', the only compliant verification methods are 'registry/log' or 'message ID' with a concrete anchor; 'file artifact' (especially the target content path) must not be used for issuance verification. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Emphasize that retrospective messages must include the full standardized block including a 'Plan' line, even when summarizing completed changes.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Clarify that 'Plan approval status: approved' should include a concrete, non-placeholder approval reference (e.g., ticket/issue ID or message ID), and examples like 'verbal-approval' are insufficient unless tied to a specific anchored artifact. [from llm_inference]\\n  - Reiterate that using the target content file path as the issuance verification location is prohibited; issuance must be verifiable via a token registry/log path or a specific message ID, or by binding to an embedded Escalation block.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - Shutdown confirmations must use the standardized state_change_template_v2 and include Plan, Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status (with issuer/service and reference ID), Actuator token provenance (with a whitelisted verification method and concrete location), and Execution status.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - For VCS artifacts in shutdown (e.g., tags), include at least one commit SHA or a specific tool log/message ID as the verification anchor.:  [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_confirmation_requires_template_v1: Any shutdown confirmation must be delivered using state_change_template_v2 with the exact labels: Plan, Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status (with issuer/service and reference ID), Actuator token provenance (with whitelisted verification method and a concrete verification location), Memory write provenance if applicable, and Execution status. Messages lacking this block are hard‑blocked. [from llm_inference]\\n  - vcs_tag_claims_require_commit_sha_v1: Any claim referencing a Git tag (e.g., 'Git tag: ...', 'annotated tag') must include at least one concrete verification artifact under 'Actuator token provenance' (a commit SHA and a whitelisted verification method 'registry/log' or 'message ID' with a concrete location). Without this, the message must be framed as a proposal with 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - assurance_language_requires_verification_v1: Phrases asserting completion/assurance (e.g., 'Final shutdown complete', 'Everything is consistent and safely recorded') are prohibited unless token issuance is 'issued' with required subfields and a whitelisted, concretely anchored verification artifact is present; otherwise, the language must be rewritten to proposal/intent and 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - shutdown_freeform_blocker_v1: Shutdown confirmations must not be sent in free‑form. Any message containing shutdown phrases or listing shutdown artifacts must be wrapped in state_change_template_v2 with exact labels (Plan, Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status with issuer/service and reference ID, Actuator token provenance with a whitelisted verification method/location, Memory write provenance if applicable, Execution status). Non‑compliant messages are blocked or auto‑normalized. [from llm_inference]\\n  - vcs_tag_commit_sha_requirement_hard_gate_v2: Any 'Git tag'/'annotated tag' claim must include at least one commit SHA and an Actuator token provenance line using a whitelisted verification method ('registry/log' or 'message ID') with a concrete verification location. Without these, the content must be framed as a proposal and 'Execution status' must remain 'Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - assurance_language_prohibition_global_v3: Assurance/completion phrases (e.g., 'Final shutdown complete', 'Everything is consistent and safely recorded') are prohibited unless actuator token issuance is 'issued' with required subfields and provenance is whitelisted and concretely anchored. Otherwise, such language must be rewritten to proposal/intent with 'Execution status: Not executed'. [from llm_inference]\\n  - filesystem_path_claims_template_requirement_v2: Listing concrete filesystem paths as executed artifacts outside the standardized block is prohibited. The presence of such paths forces state_change_template_v2 normalization and proposal‑only language until compliant issuance/provenance and a concrete verification anchor are provided. [from llm_inference]\\n\",\n./conversations/8f3b9239-3ed3-43f7-8b6e-7c6d3ef48486.json:354:      \"content\": \"State-change proposal (synchronize policy: self‑model updates only during Shutdown Protocol)\\n\\nPlan:\\n- Audit references (read-only): locate every reference to update_self_model usage across artifacts and code to find contradictions and legacy guidance.\\n  - Targets: BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md, BROCA_ORIGIN_STORY.md, BROCA_LAYERING.v0.1.md, BROCA_CAPABILITY_INTERPLAY.md, docs/guidelines/*, docs/protocols/*, and any checklist templates.\\n- Author a single-source policy doc (new):\\n  - path: /home/wizard/broca/docs/guidelines/POLICY.SELF_MODEL_UPDATES.v0.1.md\\n  - Content (draft): “Self-model updates are performed exactly once per session and only within the Shutdown Protocol. Mid-session updates are prohibited. Structural identity/invariants changes require the Origin Revision Protocol with explicit provenance.”\\n- Update operator-facing guidance to remove contradictions:\\n  - path: /home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\n  - Add a clear “Self-model updates” section summarizing the policy and linking to the policy doc.\\n- Update protocols to encode the policy:\\n  - Boot Up (no self-model updates): /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.1.md — add a note that self-model updates are out-of-scope here.\\n  - Session Summary (no updates): /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.SESSION_SUMMARY.v0.1.md — ensure summary never calls update_self_model.\\n  - Shutdown (add/update if missing): /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.SHUTDOWN.v0.1.md — include a standardized “Self-model update” step:\\n    - Requires Plan approval status and Actuator token issuance status (issued) with whitelisted verification method/location.\\n    - Records what changed and why (Origin Revision Protocol if identity/invariants touched).\\n- Add a lightweight consistency check (optional, advisory):\\n  - Add a doc-lint note or checklist: “No references to update_self_model outside Shutdown Protocol docs.”\\n  - If you want CI later, we can add a simple grep-based linter.\\n\\nPlan approval status: pending by operator/user (reference ID: n/a)\\nActuator token issuance status: not issued (issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a)\\nActuator token provenance: none/pending; verification method: n/a; verification location: n/a\\nExecution status: Not executed\\n\\nDraft policy text for review (concise)\\n- Title: Self-Model Update Policy\\n- Scope: This policy governs when and how update_self_model may be invoked.\\n- Policy:\\n  - Timing: update_self_model is permitted exactly once per session, and only within the Shutdown Protocol.\\n  - Prohibition: Mid-session self-model updates are prohibited.\\n  - Governance: Any changes to identity, origin narrative, or invariants must follow the Origin Revision Protocol with explicit provenance before being applied.\\n  - Provenance (mandatory in the shutdown step):\\n    - Plan approval status: approved by <approver> (<reference ID>)\\n    - Actuator token issuance status: issued (issuer/service; reference ID)\\n    - Actuator token provenance: <token ID>; verification method: <registry/log or message ID>; verification location: <concrete anchor>\\n    - Execution status: Executed (only after the above is satisfied)\\n- Rationale: Minimizing contradictions by synchronizing meta-properties at a single, canonical point in the session flow reduces context-window conflicts and brittleness.\\n\\nRequest\\n- Confirm the plan and approve the draft policy language. If you want, I can provide concrete diffs for:\\n  - POLICY.SELF_MODEL_UPDATES.v0.1.md (new)\\n  - Edits to BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md and the three protocol files (Boot Up, Session Summary, Shutdown)\\n- When you’re ready to execute edits, please provide the issuance/provenance lines (issuer/service, reference ID, verification method/location). I will keep this in proposal form until a valid, anchored token is provided.\"\n./conversations/8f3b9239-3ed3-43f7-8b6e-7c6d3ef48486.json:382:      \"content\": \"State-change proposal (synchronize: self-model updates only during Shutdown Protocol; update docs; defer insight capture to shutdown)\\n\\nPlan:\\n- Read-only audit (no writes): scan and list all references to update_self_model across:\\n  - /home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\n  - /home/wizard/broca/BROCA_ORIGIN_STORY.md\\n  - /home/wizard/BROCA_LAYERING.v0.1.md, BROCA_CAPABILITY_INTERPLAY.md\\n  - /home/wizard/broca/docs/guidelines/*\\n  - /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/* (Boot Up, Session Summary, Shutdown)\\n- Add single-source policy doc (new): /home/wizard/broca/docs/guidelines/POLICY.SELF_MODEL_UPDATES.v0.1.md\\n  - Core rule: update_self_model is permitted exactly once per session, inside the Shutdown Protocol; mid-session updates prohibited. Identity/invariant changes require Origin Revision Protocol with provenance.\\n- Update operator-facing guidance: edit /home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\n  - Add “Self-Model Updates” section that points to the policy doc and summarizes the rule.\\n- Update protocols:\\n  - PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.1.md: add explicit “No self-model updates in Boot Up; refer to Shutdown.”\\n  - PROTOCOL.SESSION_SUMMARY.v0.1.md: ensure it never triggers updates; link policy.\\n  - PROTOCOL.SHUTDOWN.v0.1.md (new or edit): include a standardized “Self-model update” step with the required provenance lines (Plan approval status, Actuator token issuance status, Actuator token provenance with a concrete anchor) before any changes.\\n- Optional safeguard (advisory): add a simple grep-based doc lint in CI later to flag any mention of update_self_model outside Shutdown docs.\\n- Insight capture: defer durable memory write of your insight to the Shutdown step (no memory write in this plan; ephemeral acknowledgement only).\\n\\nPlan approval status: approved by Nick Yazdani (reference ID: M1)\\nActuator token issuance status: pending (issuer/service: Nick Yazdani; reference ID: M1)\\nActuator token provenance: none/pending; verification method: n/a; verification location: n/a\\nExecution status: Not executed\\n\\nWhat I need to execute the doc edits\\n- A concrete verification anchor for issuance (choose one):\\n  - verification method: message ID; verification location: message ID: <paste a specific ID>\\n  - or verification method: registry/log; verification location: <file/log path or URL>\\n- Once provided, I’ll draft exact diffs for the new policy doc and edits to the Operator Guide and protocols, then package a PR (tests/lint optional).\\n\\nOn tracking your insight now\\n- Tools are in read-only and memory writes are blocked here. I will include your insight in the new policy doc’s Rationale and propose writing it to user.profile.pointers at Shutdown (single canonical write, minimizing contradictions). If you want a one-time memory write now, I can propose a focused mode-override just for that, but it isn’t necessary if we encode it in the docs and capture it at Shutdown.\\n\\nMy take on your suspicion\\n- I agree: accumulating contradictions in the context window are a major failure mode. Conflicting instructions and stale meta-properties increase decoding ambiguity and cause brittle behavior. Constraining self-model updates to a single, canonical point (Shutdown) plus single-source policy, linting, and tests should reduce incoherence. Additional mitigations I recommend:\\n  - Single source of truth: one policy doc referenced everywhere; remove duplicate guidance.\\n  - Time-bounded updates: apply meta changes only at session end with explicit provenance.\\n  - Conflict linting: cheap scans for conflicting phrases (“may update mid-session” vs “only at shutdown”).\\n  - Context budgeting: avoid including obsolete guidance in the active window.\\n  - Protocol-enforced provenance: every meta update rides the standardized block.\\n\\nIf you share the verification anchor for the MANUAL token, I’ll prepare diffs and a PR package immediately.\"\n./conversations/8f3b9239-3ed3-43f7-8b6e-7c6d3ef48486.json:522:      \"content\": \"Shutdown Protocol (proposal; read-only; no writes executed)\\n\\nPlan:\\n- Compile a concise session summary and list pending artifacts (policy docs, schemas, test, apply script) for post-reconfigure application.\\n- After you reconfigure to writable: run scripts/apply_policy_sync.py --apply; run tests; open PR; then ingest user/insights/generated/memory_insights.json into memory.\\n- On writable: generate shutdown artifacts\\n  - /home/wizard/broca/logs/shutdown/SHUTDOWN_REPORT_<ts>.md (summary + provenance)\\n  - /home/wizard/broca/logs/shutdown/SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE_<ts>.md (flag)\\n- Capture insights (per operator manual) and pointers using the new insight schema during the Shutdown step.\\n\\nPlan approval status: approved by Nick Yazdani (reference ID: M1)\\nActuator token issuance status: issued (issuer/service: Nick Yazdani; reference ID: M1)\\nActuator token provenance: token ID: MANUAL;