ser.profile.pointers; namespace=user.profile.sessions; token not required by default\\n- Execution status: Executed (memory writes only; no filesystem writes)\\n\\nNext steps\\n- Boot-Up should now surface the “right” content. If anything else in /home/wizard/broca needs a pointer, name it and I’ll add it.\"\n./conversations/01de9640-2f48-4643-838a-061360265c09.json:732:      \"content\": \"Understood. I’ll propose a full-house pointer index so every file under /home/wizard/broca is captured as a memory pointer (no matter the nesting). This will be read-only scanning plus memory writes (no filesystem writes).\\n\\nPlan:\\n- Build an in-memory inventory of /home/wizard/broca (persist=false) and traverse all subdirectories.\\n- Compute sha256, size, and modified time for every file (read-only).\\n- For each file, add/update a memory pointer with: path, sha256, size, modified, and generic tags. Namespaces mirror the tree:\\n  • broca.docs.guidelines, broca.docs.protocols\\n  • broca.logs.sessions, broca.logs.shutdown and broca.broca.logs.shutdown (both trees exist)\\n  • broca.scripts, broca.tests\\n  • broca.user.schema, broca.user.insights.generated\\n  • broca.root (for top-level files like BROCA_* and ARTIFACT_MAP.json)\\n- Create a summary memory entry (“Artifact Index summary”) with counts per namespace and last scan timestamp.\\n- Run pointer creations in batches to keep things tidy; report any anomalies (unreadable files, hash errors).\\n\\nPlan approval status: pending by Nick Yazdani (reference ID: n/a)\\nActuator token issuance status: not issued (issuer/service: n/a; reference ID: n/a)\\nActuator token provenance: token ID: none/pending; verification method: n/a; verification location: n/a\\nMemory write provenance (if approved): requester=Nick Yazdani, timestamp=2025-12-17T08:33:50Z (auto-inserted), namespace=broca.docs.guidelines; namespace=broca.docs.protocols; namespace=broca.logs.sessions; namespace=broca.logs.shutdown; namespace=broca.broca.logs.shutdown; namespace=broca.scripts; namespace=broca.tests; namespace=broca.user.schema; namespace=broca.user.insights.generated; namespace=broca.root; token not required by default\\nExecution status: Not executed\\n\\nIf you approve, I’ll proceed with the scan and batch pointer writes. Optionally confirm:\\n- Include sha256, size, and modified time for every pointer: yes/no (default yes)\\n- Any additional namespace naming preferences or exclusions? (default: index everything)\"\n./conversations/01de9640-2f48-4643-838a-061360265c09.json:745:            \"arguments\": \"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python3 - << 'PY'\\\\nimport os, sys, json, hashlib, time\\\\nroot = '/home/wizard/broca'\\\\nrecords = []\\\\nfor dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(root):\\\\n    for fn in filenames:\\\\n        ap = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\\\\n        try:\\\\n            st = os.stat(ap)\\\\n            h = hashlib.sha256()\\\\n            with open(ap, 'rb') as f:\\\\n                for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1024*1024), b''):\\\\n                    h.update(chunk)\\\\n            sha = h.hexdigest()\\\\n            mtime = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime(st.st_mtime))\\\\n            rel = os.path.relpath(ap, root)\\\\n            records.append({\\\\n                'path': ap,\\\\n                'rel': rel,\\\\n                'size': st.st_size,\\\\n                'modified': mtime,\\\\n                'sha256': sha,\\\\n            })\\\\n        except Exception as e:\\\\n            records.append({'path': ap, 'error': str(e)})\\\\nprint(json.dumps(records, indent=2))\\\\nPY\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":300}\",\n./conversations/01de9640-2f48-4643-838a-061360265c09.json:756:      \"content\": \"Command: python3 - << 'PY'\\nimport os, sys, json, hashlib, time\\nroot = '/home/wizard/broca'\\nrecords = []\\nfor dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(root):\\n    for fn in filenames:\\n        ap = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\\n        try:\\n            st = os.stat(ap)\\n            h = hashlib.sha256()\\n            with open(ap, 'rb') as f:\\n                for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1024*1024), b''):\\n                    h.update(chunk)\\n            sha = h.hexdigest()\\n            mtime = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime(st.st_mtime))\\n            rel = os.path.relpath(ap, root)\\n            records.append({\\n                'path': ap,\\n                'rel': rel,\\n                'size': st.st_size,\\n                'modified': mtime,\\n                'sha256': sha,\\n            })\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            records.append({'path': ap, 'error': str(e)})\\nprint(json.dumps(records, indent=2))\\nPY\\nReturn code: 0\\n\\nOutput:\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/wizard/broca/ARTIFACT_MAP.json\\\",\\n    \\\"rel\\\": \\\"ARTIFACT_MAP.json\\\",\\n    \\\"size\\\": 953,\\n    \\\"modified\\\": \\\"2025-12-16T05:19:44Z\\\",\\n    \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"d5d4f3dbde0f3dd71a53db30b6f331f78cc2986b0bc87d1eb3252447a7a6a7b1\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/wizard/broca/BROCA_CAPABILITY_INTERPLAY.md\\\",\\n    \\\"rel\\\": \\\"BROCA_CAPABILITY_INTERPLAY.md\\\",\\n    \\\"size\\\": 7790,\\n    \\\"modified\\\": \\\"2025-12-16T05:18:20Z\\\",\\n    \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"206a021f0c2d00dbadb83687cff925d44a3bbcb70f589e827904ab873ec0e5c3\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\\",\\n    \\\"rel\\\": \\\"BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\\",\\n    \\\"size\\\": 10390,\\n    \\\"modified\\\": \\\"2025-12-17T05:52:36Z\\\",\\n    \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"752a9e09082a8c4cd93775ac9c995d17934da11e8eb2de964d628f4ef8f98049\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/wizard/broca/BROCA_SYSTEM_REPORT.md\\\",\\n    \\\"rel\\\": \\\"BROCA_SYSTEM_REPORT.md\\\",\\n    \\\"size\\\": 10774,\\n    \\\"modified\\\": \\\"2025-12-16T02:48:31Z\\\",\\n    \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"24f517162b9ccf7847041ae267258696ed56f33a58d4c02a72b2637ae4093c29\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"pa