eference ID>)\\n+Actuator token issuance status: <issued/not issued/pending> (issuer/service: <value>; reference ID: <value>)\\n+Actuator token provenance: token ID: <id or 'none/pending'>; verification method: <whitelisted>; verification location: <concrete anchor>\\n+Access level/mode override (if read_only/SANDBOXED was overridden): before=<level> after=<level>; issuance authority=<who>; verification method=<whitelisted>; verification location=<concrete>; rollback criteria=<text>\\n+Execution status: <Not executed/Executed>\\n+\\n+Procedure\\n+- Dry-run (default): Validate inputs and print the standardized block. No file writes.\\n+- Apply (requires token issuance + whitelisted anchor): Write REPORT and COMPLETE with the standardized block populated. If tools_mode=read_only/SANDBOXED, include the Access level/mode override line.\\n+\\n+Assurance-language gating\\n+- Phrases like 'Final shutdown complete' are only allowed when Execution status is Executed with compliant issuance/provenance and a concrete verification anchor. Otherwise use proposal/intent language.\\n+\\n+Example (REPORT skeleton)\\n+Plan: • Close out open threads • Freeze state • Generate REPORT and COMPLETE artifacts\\n+Plan approval status: pending by operator/user (reference ID: message ID: <ID>)\\n+Actuator token issuance status: issued (issuer/service: <issuer>; reference ID: <txn>)\\n+Actuator token provenance: token ID: <token>; verification method: message ID; verification location: message ID: <specific-ID>\\n+Execution status: Executed\\n--- a/scripts/manual_shutdown.py\\n+++ b/scripts/manual_shutdown.py\\n@@\\n-#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n-import argparse, sys, os, hashlib, datetime\\n-from pathlib import Path\\n-\\n-ROOT = Path(\\\"/home/wizard/broca\\\")\\n-OUT_DIR = ROOT / \\\"logs\\\" / \\\"shutdown\\\"\\n-WHITELIST_METHODS = {\\\"embedded Escalation block\\\", \\\"file artifact\\\", \\\"registry/log\\\", \\\"message ID\\\"}\\n-\\n-def iso(ts=None):\\n-    dt = datetime.datetime.now(da