)\\ntext = p.read_text()\\ninsert = '''\\\\n## After-Storing Checklist (lightweight)\\\\nRun this immediately after creating a new memory to maximize value:\\\\n- Retrieve neighbors: use `retrieve_memories` with your core phrase; scan top 5–10.\\\\n- Link appropriately: add `elaborates`, `supports`, or `supersedes` edges to connect context.\\\\n- Tag review: ensure tags encode role and retrieval intent (e.g., `decision`, `protocol`, `summary`, `rationale`).\\\\n- Namespace check: confirm the namespace is stable and specific; adjust if misfiled.\\\\n- Importance sanity: bump to 0.7–1.0 for durable/central items; lower for incidental context.\\\\n- Provenance: set or confirm `source_type` and add a `references` link to sources when applicable.\\\\n\\\\nKeep this loop under 60–90 seconds per memory; it compounds retrieval quality over time.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n'''\\n# Insert before '## Safety & Governance'\\ntext = text.replace('\\\\n## Safety & Governance', '\\\\n' + insert + '\\\\n## Safety & Governance')\\np.write_text(text)\\nprint('OK')\\nPY\\nReturn code: 0\\n\\nOutput:\\nOK\\n\",\n./conversations/39b50e04-b870-4e26-bedf-9d7782b5b8bb.json:1760:      \"content\": \"Checklist added.\\n\\n- Updated: /home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\n- New section: “After-Storing Checklist (lightweight)”\\n  - Retrieve neighbors (top 5–10), link appropriately (elaborates/supports/supersedes)\\n  - Tag review\\n  - Namespace check\\n  - Importance sanity\\n  - Provenance set/verify and add references\\n  - Keep it under 60–90 seconds\\n\\nWant me to seed a couple of exemplar memories now and demonstrate the checklist workflow end-to-end (store → retrieve → link → tag/namespace/importance review)?\"\n./conversations/39b50e04-b870-4e26-bedf-9d7782b5b8bb.json:1840:      \"content\": \"Found 4 memory(ies) for query 'approval token file modifications EnvironmentAccess' (recency weight: 0.4):\\n\\nEpistemic confidence: average 0.82, 4 high-confidence, 0 low-confidence memories\\n\\n1. [ID: 8] After storing a new memory, immediately retrieve near neighbors and link using appropriate relation types (elaborates, supports, supersedes). Keep the review under 90 seconds.\\n   Namespace: broca.docs.protocols\\n   Tags: protocol, memory_system, linking\\n   Importance: 0.90\\n   Age: just now (created: 2025-12-16)\\n   ✓ Recent (within 24 hours)\\n\\n2. [ID: 7] Prefer EnvironmentAccess actuators over raw terminal writes for any file modifications. High-impact operations should use approval tokens (request -> approve -> token -> control_actuator).\\n   Namespace: broca.docs.guidelines\\n   Tags: guideline, governance, environment_access\\n   Importance: 0.85\\n   Age: just now (created: 2025-12-16)\\n   ✓ Recent (within 24 hours)\\n\\n3. [ID: 5] BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md created at /home/wizard/broca (v1.0, 2025-12-16). Concise workflows and best practices for memory tooling: store/retrieve/link/get-related/update/delete, linking patterns, sensible exclusions, namespacing suggestions.\\n   Namespace: broca.docs\\n   Tags: operators_guide, memory_system, broca_house\\n   Importance: 0.85\\n   Age: 32 minutes ago (created: 2025-12-16)\\n   ✓ Recent (within 24 hours)\\n\\n4. [ID: 6] Added After-Storing Checklist to BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md: retrieve neighbors, link appropriately, tag review, namespace check, importance sanity, provenance. Keep loop under 60–90 seconds.\\n   Namespace: broca.docs\\n   Tags: operators_guide, update, checklist\\n   Importance: 0.70\\n   Age: 6 minutes ago (created: 2025-12-16)\\n   ✓ Recent (within 24 hours)\\n\",\n./conversations/39b50e04-b870-4e26-bedf-9d7782b5b8bb.json:1949:            \"arguments\": \"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python - << 'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\np = Path('/home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md')\\\\ntext = p.read_text()\\\\nsnippet = '''\\\\n## Memory Linking Playbook (copy-paste ready)\\\\n\\\\nWhen to link\\\\n- supports: Evidence backs a claim or guideline\\\\n- supersedes: New decision/protocol replaces an older one (keep lineage)\\\\n- elaborates: Detailed doc expands a summary/guideline\\\\n- summarizes: Short synopsis for a longer artifact\\\\n- references: Claim or note points to a source (URL/file/path)\\\\n- contradicts: Known conflict to resolve or track\\\\n- similar_to / related_to: Non-hierarchical association; consider bidirectional\\\\n\\\\nPatterns\\\\n- Supports\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<new_id>, target_id=<evidence_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"supports\\\\\\\", strength=0.9)\\\\n\\\\n- Supersedes (lineage-preserving update)\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<new_decision_id>, target_id=<old_decision_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"supersedes\\\\\\\")\\\\n  # Optional: demote old importance or tag as deprecated via update_memory\\\\n\\\\n- Summarizes / Elaborates (pair)\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<summary_id>, target_id=<detail_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"summarizes\\\\\\\")\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<detail_id>,  target_id=<summary_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"elaborates\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n- References (cite files or URLs)\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<claim_or_note_id>, target_id=<source_ref_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"references\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n- Contradicts (record conflict for later resolution)\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<new_claim_id>, target_id=<conflicting_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"contradicts\\\\\\\", strength=0.6)\\\\n\\\\n- Similar / Related (useful for clusters; consider bidirectional)\\\\n  link_memories(source_id=<a_id>, target_id=<b_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"similar_to\\\\\\\", bidirectional=true)\\\\n\\\\nStrength guidelines\\\\n- 1.0 default for clear, strong links; 0.6–0.9 for softer associations; <0.6 sparingly.\\\\n\\\\nQuick macro after storing\\\\n1) retrieve_memories(query=\\\\\\\"<core phrase>\\\\\\\", namespaces=[\\\\\\\"<ns1>\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"<ns2>\\\\\\\"], limit=10)\\\\n2) For each good neighbor:\\\\n   - link_memories(source_id=<new_id>, target_id=<neighbor_id>, relation_type=\\\\\\\"elaborates\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"supports\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"supersedes\\\\\\\")\\\\n3) Review tags/namespace/importance; adjust via update_memory if needed\\\\n4) Add references to sources (files/URLs) when applicable\\\\n'''\\\\n# Insert before Safety & Governance if not already present\\\\nif '## Memory Linking Playbook' not in text:\\\\n    text = text.replace('\\\\\\\\n## Safety & Governance', '\\\\\\\\n' + snippet + '\\\\\\\\n## Safety & Governance')\\\\n    p.write_text(text)\\\\n    print('INSERTED')\\\\nelse:\\\\n    print('ALREADY_PRESENT')\\\\nPY\\\"}\",\n./conversations/39b50e04-b870-4e26-bedf-9d7782b5b8bb.json:1960:      \"content\": \"Command: python - << 'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np = Path('/home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md')\\ntext = p.read_text()\\nsnippet = '''\\n## Memory Linking Playbook (copy-paste ready)\\n\\nWhen to link\\n- supports: Evidence backs a claim or guideline\\n- supersedes: New decision/protocol replaces an older one (keep lineage)\\n- elaborates: Detailed doc expands a summary/guideline\\n- summarizes: Short synopsis for a longer artifact\\n- references: Claim or note points to a source (URL/file/path)\\n- contradicts: Known conflict to resolve or track\\n- similar_to / related_to: Non-hierarchical association; consider bidirectional\\n\\nPatterns\\n- Supports\\n  link_memories(source_id=<new_id>, target_id=<evidence_id>, relation_type=\\\"supports\\\", strength=0.9)\\n\\n- Supersedes (lineage-preserving update)\\n  link_memories(source_id=<new_decision_id>, target_id=<old_decision_id>, relation_type=\\\"supersedes\\\")\\n  # Optional: demote old importance or tag as deprecated via update_memory\\n\\n- Summarizes / Elaborates (pair)\\n  link_memories(source_id=<summary_id>, target_id=<detail_id>, relation_type=\\\"summarizes\\\")\\n  link_memories(source_id=<detail_id>,  target_id=<summary_id>, relation_type=\\\"elaborates\\\")\\n\\n- References (cite files or URLs)\\n  link_memories(source_id=<claim_or_note_id>, target_id=<source_ref_id>, relation_type=\\\"references\\\")\\n\\n- Contradicts (record conflict for later resolution)\\n  link_memories(source_id=<new_claim_id>, target_id=<conflicting_id>, relation_type=\\\"contradicts\\\", strength=0.6)\\n\\n- Similar / Related (useful for clusters; consider bidirectional)\\n  link_memories(source_id=<a_id>, target_id=<b_id>, relation_type=\\\"similar_to\\\", bidirectional=true)\\n\\nStrength guidelines\\n- 1.0 default for clear, strong links; 0.6–0.9 for softer associations; <0.6 sparingly.\\n\\nQuick macro after storing\\n1) retrieve_memories(query=\\\"<core phrase>\\\", namespaces=[\\\"<ns1>\\\", \\\"<ns2>\\\"], limit=10)\\n2) For each good neighbor:\\n   - link_memories(source_id=<new_id>, target_id=<neighbor_id>, relation_type=\\\"elaborates\\\"/\\\"supports\\\"/\\\"supersedes\\\")\\n3) Review tags/namespace/importance; adjust via update_memory if needed\\n4) Add references to sources (files/URLs) when applicable\\n'''\\n# Insert before Safety & Governance if not already present\\nif '## Memory Linking Playbook' not in text:\\n    text = text.replace('\\\\n## Safety & Governance', '\\\\n' + snippet + '\\\\n## Safety & Governance')\\n    p.write_text(text)\\n    print('INSERTED')\\nelse:\\n    print('ALREADY_PRESENT')\\nPY\\nReturn code: 0\\n\\nOutput:\\nINSERTED\\n\",\n./conversations/39b50e04-b870-4e26-bedf-9d7782b5b8bb.json:2000:      \"content\": \"Inserted.\\n\\n- Updated: /home/wizard/broca/BROCA_OPERATORS_GUIDE.md\\n- Section: “Memory Linking Playbook (copy-paste ready)”\\n  - When to link, patterns for supports/supersedes/summarizes/elaborates/references/contradicts/similar_to\\n  - Strength guidelines\\n  - A quick macro for post-store linking\\n\\nWant me to also add a “Supersedes” live example now (create an old decision, add a new decision that replaces it, and link them)?\"\n./conversations/39b50e04-b870-4e26-bedf-9d7782b5b8bb.json:2008:      \"content\": \"Haha yes—hi Nick. I’ve got that saved, and I know this is your laptop and my house