om filesystem; read-only reference; not copied\\\" with a timestamp\\n- If you want to preserve a sense of lineage, I can also create lightweight cross-references:\\n  - Link existing artifacts to each other where relevant (e.g., you.schema.v0.1.json may reference or imply how it relates to the insight/meta schemas).\\n\\nWhat I need from you to proceed\\n- Merge strategy:\\n  - Option A: Import as-is (reference-only) artifacts, preserving them as historical snapshots without blending their content into the current session memory.\\n  - Option B: Import and blend with current session notes (i.e., create a composite user_profile that includes both existing artifacts and this chat’s notes).\\n- Namespace preference:\\n  - Do you want strictly separate namespaces for “existing artifacts” vs. “current session artifacts” (preferred for clarity), or a unified user_profile with versioning?\\n- Any must-include or must-exclude parts from the existing artifacts?\\n  - For example, do you want to explicitly avoid storing backups, or treat them as separate references?\\n- Confirmation to proceed with token-protected write:\\n  - As per plan, I will securely read the actuator token from /home/wizard/Documents/Code/BrocaOS/.temporary_token.txt (token provenance will be recorded) and then perform the memory writes.\\n  - If you approve, I’ll produce a concise provenance note for each write (token provenance line) and a summary of what was stored and where to reference it later.\\n\\nNext steps (pending your approval)\\n- I inventory the artifacts (done) and propose the memory write plan as outlined.\\n- Please confirm:\\n  - Choose A or B for merge strategy.\\n  - Choose a preferred set of namespaces (e.g., artifacts.existing.*).\\n  - Confirm that I should proceed to read the actuator token and perform the memory writes.\\n\\nIf you’re happy with a minimal, non-destructive start, I can proceed to:\\n- Create a first pass of memory pointers for the three main artifacts (insight, 