{"level": "INFO", "logger": "broca.tools.registry", "message": "Tool execution completed: terminal", "taskName": null, "event": "tool_call_result", "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "call_Gpn0oRKj5QAasiRDOPhDh8cN", "result": {"success": true, "returncode": 0, "stdout": "# Boot-Up Protocol (BUP) v0.2\n\nPurpose\n- Extend boot semantics to include artifact-based rehydration, a formal self-consistency pass, and gated persistence.\n- Maintain artifact-first continuity: rehydrate from durable artifacts and memory pointers, not ephemeral chat.\n- Surface an Origin Revision Protocol (ORP) block if invariants drift, before mutating the self-model.\n- Produce a rehydration artifact (REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md) documenting boot results and next steps.\n\nTrigger\n- Boot of BrocaOS (start of a new session) or explicit rehydration run request.\n\nEnforcement\n- Boot runs before normal prompting. Preflight: reads-only; writes only after Plan + Approval with token provenance.\n- Self-consistency pass must complete before any state mutation, including self-model updates.\n- Invariant: artifact-first continuity; memory stores are pointers to artifacts.\n- NO_SELF_MODEL_BOOT policy remains: self-model mutations require an explicit ORP block with provenance.\n\nOverview of changes (new steps)\n- 1) load_persistence_gate(): read .shutdown_persistence.json; cryptographically verify with BROCA_TOKEN_SECRET.\n- 2) If valid: set PERSISTENCE_ENABLED = true; pull token provenance: token_id, exp, scopes.\n- 3) hydrate_pointers_and_artifacts(): load broca.session.pointer, broca.session.summary, broca.artifacts.\n- 4) hydrate_memory_graph(): rebuild memories.db/embeddings/index and memory_namespaces_index.md.\n- 5) verify_self_consistency(): lightweight invariants check; surface ORP block if drift detected.\n- 6) build_rehydration_summary(): create REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md.\n- 7) boot banner: present boot status, persistence, pointers, artifacts, next steps.\n- 8) gating posture: if persistence enabled, allow gated actions after Plan + Approval; else sandbox.\n\nSelf-consistency and ORP\n- If drift is detected, an explicit ORP block must be produced and must be approved before mutating the self-model.\n- All changes to core invariants are gated by provenance and approval templates.\n\nArtifacts\n- REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md (new artifact capturing boot results)\n- REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.json (optional sidecar)\n\nEnforcement details\n- Boot-time gates factor in: persistence gate, token provenance, and a Plan+Approval for any further writes.\n- The boot sequence itself is read-only with respect to content unless an ORP or Plan+Approval is granted.\n\nOpen threads and next steps\n- If you approve this v0.2 patch, I’ll implement the scaffold in a subsequent patch, then simulate a boot to produce a REHYDRATION_SUMMARY.v0.2.md artifact.\n\nRationale\n- This preserves a coherent self-model while improving boot reliability and auditability via artifacts and explicit provenance.\n\nEnd of PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.2.md\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x.  2 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 18 14:51 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 12 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 20 09:12 ..\n-rw-r--r--.  1 wizard wizard 3432 Dec 18 15:07 rehydration.py\n\n.writes_enabled content (first 200 chars):\nwrites_enabled: false\ndisabled_by: Nick Yazdani\njti: cb80b07534064b7283c2695fd3461b63\ntimestamp: 2025-12-19T22:40:35Z\n\n\nToken auth module listing:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x.  3 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 18 15:32 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 19 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 20 17:16 ..\n-rw-r--r--.  1 wizard wizard  820 Dec 18 15:32 BROCA_TOKEN_GUIDE.md\n-rw-r--r--.  1 wizard wizard 2029 Dec 19 22:10 cli.py\n-rw-r--r--.  1 wizard wizard 1323 Dec 18 15:32 defaults.py\n-rw-r--r--.  1 wizard wizard  549 Dec 19 22:10 __init__.py\ndrwxr-xr-x.  2 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 19 22:10 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r--.  1 wizard wizard 3912 Dec 19 22:10 token.py\n\nToken auth README or docs if present:\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard  820 Dec 18 15:32 broca/token_auth/BROCA_TOKEN_GUIDE.md\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard 2029 Dec 19 22:10 broca/token_auth/cli.py\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard 1323 Dec 18 15:32 broca/token_auth/defaults.py\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard  549 Dec 19 22:10 broca/token_auth/__init__.py\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard 3912 Dec 19 22:10 broca/token_auth/token.py\n\nbroca/token_auth/__pycache__:\ntotal 28\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 19 22:10 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 3 wizard wizard 4096 Dec 18 15:32 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard 3214 Dec 19 22:10 cli.cpython-313.pyc\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard 2300 Dec 18 15:38 defaults.cpython-313.pyc\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard  673 Dec 19 22:10 __init__.cpython-313.pyc\n-rw-r--r--. 1 wizard wizard 5959 Dec 19 22:10 token.cpython-313.pyc\n\nGit status summary:\n## main...origin/main [ahead 14]\n M broca/storage/json_storage.py\n M broca/tests/conftest.py\n M broca/tests/test_optimization_daemon.py\n M broca/tests/test_session.py\n M broca/tests/test_session_storage_system_prompt.py\n M broca/tests/test_session_tools.py\n M broca/tests/test_terminal_tool.py\n", "stderr": "ls: cannot access 'broca/bootup': No such file or directory\n", "command": "set -euo pipefail\n# Inspect boot protocol and related bootup tooling (read-only)\nsed -n '1,200p' /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.2.md\nprintf \"\\n---\\n\\n\"\nsed -n '200,400p' /home/wizard/broca/docs/protocols/PROTOCOL.BOOT_UP.v0.2.md || true\nprintf \"\\n---\\n\\n\"\nls -la /home/wizard/broca/bootup || true\nls -la broca/bootup || true\nprintf \"\\n.writes_enabled content (first 200 chars):\\n\"; head -c 200 .writes_enabled; echo\nprintf \"\\nToken auth module listing:\\n\"; ls -la broca/token_auth\nprintf \"\\nToken auth README or docs if present:\\n\"; ls -la broca/token_auth/* 2>/dev/null | sed -n 'p' | head -n 20\n# Show git status (read-only)\nprintf \"\\nGit status summary:\\n\"; git status --porcelain=v1 -b"}, "formatted_result": "Command: set -euo pipefail\n# Inspect boot protocol and rel